hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - and he raised the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: 'Whoever makes an image will be charged to breathe a soul into it, and he will not breathe into it; whoever claims to have seen a dream falsely will be charged to tie a knot between two grains of barley, and he will not tie it; and whoever listens to the talk of people who flee from it, molten lead will be poured into his ear on the Day of Resurrection.'"
"602","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to me, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, said: 'Whoever among you knows that I have power to forgive sins, I forgive him and I do not care, so long as he does not associate anything with Me.'"
"603","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to me: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, that Ibn Abbas said to a man: Shall I not present you with a hadith that will delight you? The man said: Yes indeed, O Abu Abbas, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: Recite 'Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the Dominion,' memorize it, teach it to your family, all your children, the youngsters of your house, and your neighbors; for it is the savior, and it is the defender - it will plead and dispute on the Day of Resurrection before its Lord on behalf of its reciter, and seek from its Lord that He save him from the Fire if it was in his heart. And Allah saves its companion through it from the punishment of the grave. Ibrahim said: my father said: Ikrimah said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I would love that it be in the heart of every person of my Ummah.'"
"604","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'While I was a boy with the children, we went to a place, and they seated me upon their belongings and went away from me. While I was sitting, I saw two birds descending from the sky; one sat at my right and the other at my left. I heard the one at my right saying to his companion: Is this the one to whom we have been sent? He said: Yes. While I was thus, my companions, the children, came toward me; when they saw them, the two went up to the sky.'"
"605","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The companions of Musa who crossed the sea were twelve tribes, and in each path were twelve thousand, all of them children of Ya'qub the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).'"
"606","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of his and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I want you to witness a charity I am giving to this son of mine. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Do you have another son besides him?' He said: Yes. He said: 'Did you give him the same as you gave this one?' He said: No. He said: 'Then I will not bear witness.'"
"607","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Ma'idah and Surah al-Tawbah in his sermon, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Declare lawful what Allah has made lawful in them, and declare unlawful what Allah has made unlawful in them.'"
"608","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers while resident - so should I not combine them while traveling?"
"609","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers while resident and while traveling."
"610","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink one day, drinking in three breaths. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you drank water in three breaths. He said: 'Yes, it is more wholesome, more healing, and more pleasant.'"
"611","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a very old man unable to perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Yes, perform Hajj in place of your father.'"
"612","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while he was ill, and circumambulated the House upon a camel, with a curved staff with him; whenever he passed the Stone he touched it with it. When he finished his circumambulation, he made the camel kneel, then prayed two rak'ahs."
"613","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not yet departed until the sun declined, he would pray Zuhr and Asr together; and when he departed before the sun declined, he would delay them until he prayed both at the time of Asr."
"614","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to quote verses of poetry as examples."
"615","Ali ibn Asim narrated to me, from Abu Ali al-Rahabi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever takes an orphan from among the Muslims under his care, feeding and giving him drink until Allah enriches him from him, Allah will certainly make Paradise obligatory for him - unless he does a deed that is not forgiven. And whomever Allah takes his two precious ones from, and he is patient and seeks reward, Allah will certainly make Paradise obligatory for him.' They said: What are his two precious ones? He said: 'His two eyes. And whoever maintains three daughters, spending on them and treating them well until they leave or die, Allah will certainly make Paradise obligatory for him - unless he does a deed that is not forgiven.' A Bedouin man from among the emigrants called out to him: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: 'And two.' And when Ibn Abbas would narrate this hadith, he would say: This, by Allah, is among the rare and precious hadiths."
"616","Abu al-Walid informed me: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd and Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until snoring was heard from him, then he stood and prayed without performing ablution. Ikrimah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was protected."
"617","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Muhammad ibn Muslim informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones: the forehead - then Tawus would say, passing his hand over his nose like this - the two hands, the two knees, and the two feet; and not to tuck up hair nor garment."
"618","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed prayer while traveling as two rak'ahs and while resident as four. As you pray before and after it in residence, so pray before and after it if you wish while traveling."
"619","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Abd al-Karim informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman in her litter, and she took the child with one of her hands and said: O Prophet of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: 'Yes, and for you is reward.'"
"620","Fahd ibn Awf narrated to me: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two graves and said: 'They are both being punished in their graves, and they are not being punished for something major: one of them used to spread gossip, and the other did not guard against urine.' Then he took a palm stalk, broke it into two pieces, planted a piece at the head of each of them, and said: 'Perhaps it will be lightened for them until these two dry out.'"
"621","Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate at night: 'O Allah, to You is praise; You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is in them. To You is praise; You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and what is in them. To You is praise; You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and what is in them. Your word is truth, Your promise is truth, meeting You is truth, Paradise is truth, Hell is truth, and the Hour is truth. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I turn, by You I dispute, and to You I bring judgment. Forgive me what I have done before and in secret, what I have delayed and declared. You are Allah; there is no god but You.'"
"622","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had himself cupped while in ihram."
"623","Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The first thing with which the believing servant is rewarded after his death is that all those who followed his funeral are forgiven.'"
"624","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'We, the assembly of Prophets, have been commanded to delay our suhur and to hold our right hands over our left in prayer.'"
"625","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Talhah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O people, seek treatment; for Allah, mighty and exalted is He, has not created a disease except that He has created for it a cure - except al-Sam; and al-Sam is death.'"
"626","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Talhah informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: 'When one of you eats food that is licked with the fingers, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked.'"
"627","Ya'la informed us: Talhah informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The best of you are the best of you in character.'"
"628","Sa'id ibn Amir informed us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Allah hears whoever praises Him,' he would say: 'O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will after that.'"
"629","Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When one of you eats food, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked; for the last of the food contains blessing.'"
"630","He said: And Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Do not lift the bowl until you lick it or have it licked; for the last of the food contains blessing.'"
"631","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Mubarak ibn Hassan, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of our companions is best? He said: 'The one whose sight reminds you of Allah, whose speech increases you in knowledge, and whose deed reminds you of the Hereafter.'"
"632","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is a very old man who never performed Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: 'If your father owed a debt, would you settle it on his behalf?' He said: Yes. He said: 'Then perform Hajj on his behalf.'"
"633","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, in which were six pillars; he stood at each pillar supplicating or seeking forgiveness, and did not pray."
"634","Abu al-Walid narrated to me: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Qays, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the last Isha one night until the people slept, then woke, then slept, then woke, then slept, then woke. Then Umar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the prayer, the prayer. So he stood and prayed, and no ablution was mentioned."
"635","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Hushaym narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing, he would say: 'O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will after that; O People of praise and glory, none can withhold what You give, none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You.'"
"636","Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Jud'ani narrated to me, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O Ibn Abbas, guard Allah and He will guard you; guard Allah and you will find Him before you. Know Allah in ease and He will know you in hardship. Know that what befell you could never have missed you, and what missed you could never have befallen you; and that if all creatures gathered to give you something Allah did not will to give you, they could not do so - or to avert from you something Allah willed to give you, they could not do so. The Pen has dried upon what is to be until the Day of Resurrection. When you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah; for victory comes with patience, relief with distress, and indeed with hardship comes ease.'"
"637","Abu Nu'aym, Sulayman ibn Dawud, and Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'I was aided by al-Saba (the easterly wind), and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur (the westerly wind).'"
"638","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Isra'il ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss the Yamani Corner and place his cheek upon it."
"639","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muslim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a shirt with short sleeves and length."
"640","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, he said: I heard Mujahid narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man and saw his thigh exposed. He said: 'Cover your thigh, for a man's thigh is part of his nakedness.'"
"641","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever among you is unable to endure the night in worship, is miserly with wealth to spend it, and is cowardly toward the enemy to fight him - let him increase in remembrance of Allah.'"
"642","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Most of the punishment of the grave is on account of urine; so keep yourselves clean of urine.'"
"643","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid and Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'I have been given five - and I do not say it out of pride: I have been sent to the red and the black; the earth has been made for me a means of purification and a mosque; war booty has been made lawful for me though it was not lawful for anyone before me; I have been aided by terror cast a month's journey ahead of me; and I have been given intercession, which I have reserved for my Ummah until the Day of Resurrection - and it shall, Allah willing, reach whoever does not associate anything with Allah.'"
"644","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The people came with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims, and he commanded them, so they made it Umrah. Then he said: 'Had I known beforehand what I know now, I would not have done that - but Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.' Then he interlaced his fingers. So all the people exited ihram except those who had sacrificial animals with them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sacrificial animals with him, Talhah had sacrificial animals with him, and Ali came from Yemen. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'For what did you enter ihram?' He said: For what you entered ihram. He said: 'Do you have a sacrificial animal with you?' He said: No. He said: 'Then remain as you are, for you have a third of my sacrificial animals.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a hundred sacrificial animals with him."
"645","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in Ramadan from Madinah with ten thousand Muslims toward Makkah, fasting, and they fasted - until when he reached al-Kadid, between Usfan and Qudayd, he broke his fast, and the Muslims broke their fast with him, and they did not fast anything of the rest of Ramadan. Al-Zuhri said: Breaking the fast was the later of the two matters. Al-Zuhri said: What is taken from the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the later, then the later. Al-Zuhri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Makkah by morning when thirteen nights of Ramadan had passed."
"646","Uthman ibn Umar informed us: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most generous of people, and he was most generous in Ramadan when Jibril, peace be upon him, would meet him; he would meet him every night in Ramadan reviewing the Qur'an with him. When Jibril, peace be upon him, met him, he was more generous than the wind sent forth."
"647","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to present the Book to Jibril, peace be upon him, in every Ramadan. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose in the morning following the night in which he presented what he presented, he would rise more generous than the wind sent forth, and he would not be asked for anything but that he gave it. When the month came after which he passed away, he presented it to him twice."
"648","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of the Conquest in Ramadan and fasted; when he was at al-Kadid, he broke his fast. What is taken from his affair is the latest, and the latest abrogated the earliest."
"649","Abu Asim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk, then rinsed his mouth and said: 'It has greasiness.'"
"650","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing four creatures: the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, and the shrike."
"651","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep belonging to Maymunah and said: 'Why did you not make use of its hide?' They said: How, O Messenger of Allah, when it is dead? He said: 'Only its flesh has been forbidden.'"
"652","Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim informed us: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrating from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The best of companions are four, the best of detachments are four hundred, the best of armies are four thousand; and twelve thousand shall not be defeated out of fewness.'"
"653","Abu Nu'aym narrated to me, he said: Abu Shaybah narrated to me, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray twenty rak'ahs in Ramadan and pray Witr with three."
"654","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched Abdullah ibn Rawahah, Ja'far, and Zayd ibn Harithah toward Syria. Ibn Rawahah stayed behind, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'What kept you back?' He said: I will gather my things, then set out. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'A morning march in the cause of Allah, or an evening one, is better than this world and what is in it.' So Abdullah set out departing."
"655","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came during the truce before the treaty between him and them, while the polytheists were at the door of al-Nadwah on the side of al-Hijr, and they had said among themselves that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions were afflicted with hardship and emaciation. When they touched the Stone, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: 'They have said that you are afflicted with hardship and emaciation, so walk briskly for three circuits, so they see that you have strength.' When they touched the Stone, they lifted their feet and walked briskly. Then some of them said to others: Did you not claim they were afflicted with hardship and emaciation? Yet they are not content with walking, but hasten running."
"656","Ibn Abi Shaybah informed me: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abdullah ibn Rawahah on a detachment, and that coincided with Friday. His companions set out in the morning, but Abdullah said: I shall stay back and pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then catch up with my companions. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, he said: 'What prevented you from setting out in the morning with your companions?' He said: I wished to attend Friday with you, then catch up with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Had you spent all that is on earth, you would not attain the merit of their morning march.'"
"657","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'The words of relief: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Almighty; there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no god but He, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Noble Throne.'"
"658","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi narrated to them, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with them or say them at times of distress: 'There is no god but Allah, the Almighty, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Noble Throne.'"
"659","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Wasiti, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr, then sleep while prostrating until he snored or breathed heavily, then rise for prayer. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have slept. He said: 'Ablution is obligatory only upon one who sleeps lying down; for when he does so, his joints relax.'"
"660","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas: When something troubled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: 'There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Almighty; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the seven heavens, Lord of the earth, and Lord of the Noble Throne' - then he would supplicate."
"661","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us: my father narrated to me that Abu Harun al-Ghitrif narrated to him that Abu al-Sha'tha narrated to him that Ibn Abbas narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him: The Trustworthy Spirit narrated to him that Allah, blessed and exalted is He, has decreed that the deeds of the servant be brought on the Day of Resurrection - his good deeds and his evil deeds - and some be set off against others. If a single good deed remains for him, Allah will extend for him in Paradise as He wills. Ibrahim said: my father said: I said to Abu Salamah ibn Yazdad: What if the good deed is gone and nothing remains? He said: 'Those are they from whom We accept the best of what they did and overlook their evil deeds, among the companions of Paradise - the true promise which they were promised.'"
"662","Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to travel between Makkah and Madinah fearing none but Allah, mighty and exalted is He, praying two rak'ahs until he returned to his family."
"663","Mus'ab ibn Miqdam al-Khath'ami narrated to us: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled between Makkah and Madinah, praying two rak'ahs, fearing - or dreading - none but Allah, mighty and exalted is He."
"664","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When Allah, mighty and exalted is He, drowned Pharaoh, he said: I believe that there is no god but He in whom the Children of Isra'il believe. So Jibril said: O Muhammad, had you seen me taking mud from the sea and stuffing it into his mouth, fearing that mercy would reach him.'"
"665","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no servant but that he errs or intends an error - except Yahya ibn Zakariyya, peace be upon him. And no servant should say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta.'"
"666","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it as much as you wish.'"
"667","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited - in what the sleeper sees - by two angels; one sat at his feet and the other at his head. The one at his feet said to the one at his head: Strike a parable for this man and for his Ummah. He said: 'The example of him and his Ummah is that of traveling people who reached the edge of a desert, having neither provisions to cross the desert nor to return. While they were thus, a well-groomed man in a fine Yemeni cloak came to them and said: What if I bring you to green meadows and full cisterns - will you follow me? They said: Yes. So he set out with them and brought them to green meadows and full cisterns, and they ate, drank, and grew fat. He said to them: Did I not find you in that state, and you promised me that if I brought you to green meadows and full cisterns you would follow me? They said: Yes. He said: Ahead of you are meadows greener than this and cisterns fuller than these, so follow me. One group said: He has spoken the truth; by Allah, we shall surely follow him. And one group said: We are content with this; we shall stay here.'"
"668","Uthman ibn Umar informed us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id ibn Khalid, from Isma'il ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Dhu'ayb, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: 'Shall I not inform you of the person with the finest station? A man holding the bridle of his horse in the cause of Allah until he dies or is killed. Shall I not inform you of the one next to him? A man in a mountain pass among these passes who establishes prayer, gives zakat, and keeps away from the evils of people. Shall I not inform you of the person with the worst station? The one who is asked by Allah yet does not give for His sake.'"
"669","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Shu'bah informed us, from Hajib ibn Umar, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj, from Ibn Abbas, who said: 'Ashura is the ninth day.' I said: Did Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast it thus? He said: Yes."
"670","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Hajib ibn Umar informed us, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj, he said: I came to Ibn Abbas while he was leaning his back against the enclosure of Zamzam, and I said: Inform me about Ashura. He said: About which aspect of it do you ask? I said: About fasting it. He said: 'When you see the crescent of Muharram, count nine, then rise in the morning fasting.' I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast it thus? He said: Yes."
"671","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If I live until next year, Allah willing, I shall surely fast the ninth day' - meaning Ashura."
"672","Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Husayn, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he stood, performed ablution, used the tooth-stick, and recited this verse until he finished it: 'Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day are signs for those of understanding' - until he recited these verses to the end of the surah. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, then returned and slept until I heard his breathing. Then he stood, performed ablution, used the tooth-stick, prayed two rak'ahs, then prayed Witr with three."
"673","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Salim ibn Ubayd informed us, from Abu Abdullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no man on earth who dies with a mustard seed's weight of pride in his heart except that Allah will place him in the Fire.' When Abdullah ibn Qays al-Ansari heard that, he wept. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O Abdullah ibn Qays, why do you weep?' He said: Because of your words. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Rejoice, for you are in Paradise.' Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and he went out fighting in it and was killed as a martyr. He repeated it three times. Then a man from the Ansar said: O Prophet of Allah, I love to beautify myself with my sword strap, by washing my garments of dirt, and with fine straps and sandals. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'That is not what I mean. Pride is only scorning the truth and belittling people.' He said: O Prophet of Allah, what is scorning the truth and belittling people? He said: 'Scorning the truth is that you have wealth owed to you by a man, and he denies it, claiming nothing is due upon him; then a man commands him to fear Allah, mighty and exalted is He, saying: Fear Allah - whereupon he says: If I have not feared Allah until you command me, then I am ruined. That is the one who scorns the truth.' And he asked him about belittling people. He said: 'It is the one who comes with his nose held high; when he sees the weak and poor among people, he does not greet them nor sit with them, despising them. That is the one who belittles people.' Thereupon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever raises his garment, patches his sandal, rides the donkey, visits the slave when he is ill, and milks the sheep has freed himself of haughtiness.'"
"674","Yazid informed us: Abdullah ibn Dukayn informed us: Qays al-Masir narrated to us: Dawud al-Basri narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Every believer has a sin he returns to time after time, or a sin he does not abandon until he dies or the Hour comes upon him. The believer is created sinful, oft-tried, oft-erring, forgetful; when reminded, he remembers.'"
"675","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to me: Hisham ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, who said: I knew Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, may Allah have mercy on him, when he was our governor in Madinah - a young man of stout build and full body. When he became caliph and endured the toil and worry he endured, his condition changed, and I kept looking at him, hardly turning my gaze away. He said: O Ibn Ka'b, you look at me with a look you never looked at me before. He said: I said: It amazes me. He said: What amazes you? He said: Your color that has changed, your hair that has fallen, and your body that has grown thin. He said: How would it be if you saw me after three days, when my eyeballs flow upon my cheeks, and my nostrils and mouth flow with pus and worms - you would find it even more unfamiliar. Repeat to me a hadith you once narrated to me from Ibn Abbas. He said: I said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me - and he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: 'Everything has a nobility, and the noblest of gatherings is that faced toward the qiblah. Company is only with trust. Do not pray behind one who sleeps nor one who converses. Kill the snake and the scorpion even if you are in prayer. Do not cover walls with garments. Whoever looks into his brother's book without his permission, it is as if he looks into the Fire. Whoever wishes to be the noblest of people, let him fear Allah; whoever wishes to be the strongest of people, let him rely upon Allah; whoever wishes to be the richest of people, let him trust what is in Allah's Hand more than what is in his own hand. Shall I not inform you of the worst of you?' They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'One who stays alone, withholds his help, and beats his slave.' He said: 'Shall I inform you of worse than this?' They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'One who hates people and whom people hate.' He said: 'Shall I inform you of worse than this?' They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'One who does not overlook a stumble, nor accept an excuse, nor forgive a sin.' He said: 'Shall I inform you of worse than this?' They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'One whose good is not hoped for and whose evil is not safe from. Indeed, Isa son of Maryam stood among his people and said: O Children of Isra'il, do not speak wisdom before the ignoramus, lest you wrong it; nor withhold it from its people, lest you wrong them; do not wrong, nor repay a wrongdoer with wrong, lest your merit be nullified before your Lord. O Children of Isra'il, matters are three: a matter whose rightness is clear, so follow it; a matter whose error is clear, so avoid it; and a matter disputed over, so refer it to its scholar.'"
"676","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Abdullah ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while they were advancing loans for fruits for years ahead. He said: 'Advance loans in a known measure and known weight, until a known term.'"
"677","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Sinan, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Aqra' ibn Habis asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year or once? He said: 'No, rather once; whoever does more, it is voluntary.'"
"678","Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Aban, from Shahr, from Ibn Abbas - raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: 'The Opening of the Book equals two-thirds of the Qur'an.'"
"679","Yusuf ibn Buhlul narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When your companions were struck at Uhud, Allah placed their souls in the bellies of green birds that visit the rivers of Paradise, eat of its fruits, and shelter in lamps of gold in the shade of the Throne. When they found the sweetness of their drink, food, and resting place, they said: Would that our brothers knew what Allah has done for us, so they would not lose interest in jihad nor hold back in war. Allah, mighty and exalted is He, said: I shall convey it to them from you. So Allah, mighty and exalted is He, revealed: 'And do not think those killed in the cause of Allah are dead' - until the account of the martyrs was completed."
"680","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Yahya al-Jabir, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about one who deliberately kills a believer. He said: 'His recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah is angry with him' - the verse. It was said to him: What if he repents, believes, does righteous deeds, then is guided? Ibn Abbas said: How can he be guided? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'May his mother be bereaved of him - one who deliberately kills a believer will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying his head in one of his hands, seizing his companion with the other hand, his jugular veins gushing blood before the Throne of the Most Merciful, mighty and exalted is He, saying: Ask this one for what he killed me. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it was revealed and no verse abrogated it until your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, and no proof was revealed after it.'"
"681","Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mu'min ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to me, he said: Najdah narrated to me that he asked Ibn Abbas about the saying of Allah, mighty and exalted is He: 'If you do not march forth, He will punish you with a painful punishment.' He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a clan of the Arab clans to march forth, but they held back from him, so rain was withheld from them - and that was their punishment: 'If you do not march forth, He will punish you with a painful punishment.'"
"682","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'My Lord came to me tonight in the finest form - I think he said: in a dream - and said to me: O Muhammad, do you know concerning what the Highest Assembly disputes? I said: No. So He placed His Hand between my shoulders until I felt its coolness between my breasts - or my throat - and I knew what is in the heavens and the earth. He said to me: O Muhammad, do you know concerning what the Highest Assembly disputes? I said: Yes - concerning expiations. And expiations are: remaining in the mosques after prayers, walking on foot to congregations, and performing ablution thoroughly in hardship. Whoever does that lives well, dies well, and is free of sin as on the day his mother bore him. And say, O Muhammad, when you pray: O Allah, I ask You for good deeds, abandoning evils, loving the poor; and when You intend trial for Your servants, take me to You without trial. And the highest ranks are: spreading peace, feeding food, and praying at night while people sleep.'"
"683","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among a group of his Companions from the Ansar, a star was shot and shone. He said: 'What did you say when such as this occurred in the pre-Islamic age?' They said: We used to say: A great one is born, or a great one dies. He said: 'It is not shot for anyone's death nor life. But when our Lord, blessed and exalted is He, decrees a matter in heaven, the bearers of the Throne glorify Him, then the inhabitants of heaven glorify, and every heaven's inhabitants glorify, until the glorification reaches this heaven. The inhabitants of heaven ask the bearers of the Throne: What did your Lord say? They inform them. The inhabitants of each heaven ask the inhabitants of another heaven, until the news reaches this heaven, and the jinn snatch and are pelted. What they bring is true, but they mix falsehood into it and add to it.' I said to al-Zuhri: Were they pelted in the pre-Islamic age? He said: Yes. I said: What about His saying: 'And we used to sit therein in stations for hearing' - the verse? He said: It was made severe and its affair intensified when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent."
"684","Shaddad ibn Hakim and Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Two blessings in which many people are cheated: health and free time.'"
"685","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There are three traits: whoever is free of them, Allah the Almighty forgives whatever is besides that for whomever He wills: whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, and was not a sorcerer who follows sorcerers, and did not bear malice against his brother."
"686","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Malik ibn Khayr al-Ziyadi, that Malik ibn Sad al-Tujibi narrated to him that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad, indeed Allah the Almighty has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, its pourer, and the one for whom it is poured."
"687","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two Eids, in the first rakah the Opening of the Book and Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and in the second the Opening of the Book and Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."
"688","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me; no believer in this world asks Allah for me except that I will be a witness or an intercessor, or a witnessing intercessor, for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"689","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you, when he intends to come to his wife, says: In the name of Allah, O Allah, keep Satan away from me and keep Satan away from what You grant us, and a child is decreed between them, Satan will never harm him."
"690","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah and from Amr ibn Dinar, from Said ibn al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out from relieving himself, then he wanted to eat, and it was said: Will you not perform ablution? He said: I have only been commanded with ablution for prayer."
"691","Jafar ibn Awn informed us, Said ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into the Fire and most of its people were women, and I looked into Paradise and most of its people were the poor."
"692","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was in the house of Maymunah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray at night, so I stood on his left, and he took my hand and placed me on his right, then he prayed thirteen rakahs including the two rakahs of Fajr, and I estimated his standing in each rakah to be about the length of O you wrapped in garments."
"693","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has wealth sufficient to convey him to Hajj and does not perform Hajj, or has wealth in which zakat is due and does not pay its zakat, will ask to return at death. They said: O Ibn Abbas, we used to think this was only for the disbeliever. He said: I shall recite to you Quran about that, then he recited: O you who believe, let not your wealth and your children divert you from the remembrance of Allah, until he reached: Then he would give charity and be among the righteous."
"694","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Abdullah ibn Musawir: I heard Ibn Abbas mention Ibn al-Zubayr and speak of his miserliness, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The believer is not one who eats his fill while his neighbor beside him is hungry."
"695","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom the earth will split open, and I do not say it out of pride."
"696","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to me, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu al-Safar narrating from Said ibn Shufayy, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whenever he left his house or his family, continued praying two rakahs until he returned."
"697","Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fought any people until he had called them."
"698","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Imran ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Tamim narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in the end of time a people nicknamed al-Rafidah; they reject Islam and cast it off; kill them, for they are polytheists."
"699","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari: I asked Ibn Abbas about selling palm trees, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling palm trees until some of it is eaten, or until it is weighed. He said: I said to those sitting with him: What is meant by weighed? He said: Estimated."
"700","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Imran al-Sulami, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Quraysh said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Supplicate your Lord for us to make al-Safa gold for us; if it becomes gold for us we will believe in you. So he supplicated his Lord, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Your Lord conveys peace to you and says: If you wish, it will become gold for them, but whoever disbelieves among them I will punish with a punishment with which I have punished no one in the worlds; and if you wish, I will open for them the door of repentance and mercy. He said: O Lord, the door of repentance and mercy."
"701","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Zirr, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I find in myself something of whispering; I would rather be turned to charcoal than speak of it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great; praise be to Allah who has reduced his affair to whispering."
"702","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Shall I not inform you of the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then he called for water and performed ablution washing once each time."
"703","Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Jibril led me at the House twice: he led me in Zuhr when the sun had declined, when it was like the measure of a sandal strap, then he led me in Asr when the shadow of everything became like it, and he led me in Maghrib when the fasting person breaks his fast, and he led me in Isha when the twilight disappeared, and he led me in Fajr when food and drink become forbidden for the fasting person; then he led me in Zuhr when the shadow of everything became like it, at the time of Asr of the previous day, and he led Asr when the shadow of everything became twice it, and he led me in Maghrib when the fasting person breaks his fast, and he led me in Isha when the first third of the night had passed, and he led me in Fajr when it became bright, then he turned to me and said: O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you; the time is between these two times."
"704","Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The name of Juwayriyah was Barrah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named her Juwayriyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, then he left her after praying Fajr and sat until mid-morning rose, then he came while she was in her place of prayer. She said: I have remained after you, O Messenger of Allah, constantly engaged. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have said words after you which, if weighed against what you have said, would outweigh them: Glory be to Allah, the number of His creation; glory be to Allah, the pleasure of His Self; glory be to Allah, the weight of His Throne; glory be to Allah, the ink of His words - three times."
"705","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Mandal narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given a gift while people are with him, they are partners with him in it."
"706","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, who said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to me, who said: Said ibn Yasar informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that much of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakahs of Fajr was: We believe in Allah and what was sent down to us, the verse, in the first rakah, and in the other rakah: We believe in Allah, and bear witness that we are Muslims."
"707","Abu Nuaym narrated to me, al-Bara ibn Abdullah narrated to us, who said: Abu Nadrah narrated to me that Ibn Abbas was on the pulpit of Basrah on Friday and said in his sermon: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge at the end of his prayer from four things, saying: I seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire, and I seek refuge with Allah from trials, the apparent and the hidden thereof, and I seek refuge with Allah from the one-eyed liar."
"708","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I was told that Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies addicted to wine will meet Allah the Almighty like a worshipper of idols."
"709","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, without travel or rain. They said: O Abu Abbas, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intend by that, or why did he do that? He said: He intended latitude for his ummah."
"710","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what the sleeper sees, at midday, disheveled and dusty, with him a bottle containing blood. I said: O Prophet of Allah, what is this? He said: This is the blood of al-Husayn and his companions; I have continued gathering them since today. He said: That day was counted and they found that he was killed on that day."
"711","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lightest in punishment among the people of the Fire is Abu Talib; on his feet are two sandals of fire by which his brain boils."
"712","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was with my father at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was as if turning away from my father. When we stood up, my father said to me: O my son, did you not see your cousin as if turning away from me? I said: O father, there was a man with him privately conversing with him. Al-Abbas returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, I said to Abdullah such and such, and he claims there was a man with you conversing with you; was there anyone with you? He said: O Abdullah, did you see him? He said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him."
"713","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is as if I am looking at a black bow-legged man uprooting it stone by stone, meaning the Kabah."
"714","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abdullah, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns a branch of knowledge from the stars has learned a branch of magic."
"715","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Salih ibn Hassan al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you ask Allah, ask Him with the palms of your hands and do not ask Him with the backs of them, and wipe your faces with them."
"716","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid informed me, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Jad Abu Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what he narrates from his Lord. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord is Merciful; whoever intends a good deed before doing it, one good deed is written for him, and if he does it, ten to seven hundred to many multiples are written for him; and whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, a good deed is written for him, and if he does it, one is written against him, or something like this; and none perishes at the hands of Allah except one doomed to perish."
"717","Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Talq ibn Qays, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: My Lord, help me and do not help against me, grant me victory and do not grant victory against me, plan for me and do not plan against me, guide me and make guidance easy for me, and grant me victory over whoever transgresses against me. My Lord, make me grateful to You, remembering You, fearful of You, obedient to You, humble toward You, oft-returning, turning to You. My Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, make firm my proof, make my tongue truthful, guide my heart, and remove the rancor of my heart."
"718","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person whose death has not yet come and says: I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to cure you, seven times, he will be cured."
"719","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Abu Hadir al-Azdi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Sacrificial camels became scarce in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he commanded the people to use cattle."
"720","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, who said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Mihran Abu Safwan, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you intends Hajj, let him hasten."
"721","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Harith ibn Fudayl, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are upon Bariq, a river at the gate of Paradise, in a green dome; their provision comes to them from Paradise morning and evening."
"722","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever buys a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and whoever buys pollinated date-palms, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."
"723","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw upon Umar a white shirt and said: Is this shirt of yours new or washed? He said: Rather washed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Wear new, live praised, and die a martyr."
"724","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are like a hundred camels among which a man can hardly find a riding camel."
"725","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man of the Ansar who was admonishing his brother about modesty, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for modesty is part of faith."
"726","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion, there is no partner for You. Ibn Umar said: And I added: Here I am, here I am, at Your service; here I am, and good is in Your hands, and longing and striving are toward You."
"727","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim man has a right that three nights pass over him except that his will is with him. Ibn Umar said: Never did three nights pass over me except that my will was with me."
"728","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed Jumuah, would enter his house and pray two rakahs."
"729","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given the Quran and he stands with it during hours of the night and hours of the day, and a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends from it during hours of the night and hours of the day."
"730","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man dies, his seat is shown to him morning and evening: if he is of the people of Paradise, then Paradise; and if he is of the people of the Fire, then the Fire. He said: Then it is said: This is your seat to which you will be raised on the Day of Resurrection."
"731","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Khalid ibn al-Walid, I think to Banu Jadhimah, and he called them to Islam, but they did not do well in saying it, and they began saying: We have left our religion, we have left our religion. And Khalid set about killing and capturing them. He said: Then he handed to each man among us a captive, until one morning he commanded us and said: Let each man among you kill his captive. Ibn Umar said: I said: By Allah, I will not kill my captive, nor will any man among my companions kill his captive. He said: Then we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what Khalid had done was mentioned to him. He said: He raised his hands and said: O Allah, I disavow to You what Khalid has done - two or three times."
"732","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten rakahs which he used to pray by night and day: two rakahs before Zuhr and two after it, two after Jumuah, two after Maghrib, and two after Isha. He said: And Hafsah told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs before Fajr."
"733","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad al-Zuhri narrated to me, from his father, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The keys of the unseen are five: Indeed with Allah is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die; indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"734","Ahmad ibn Yunus informed me, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until you hear the call of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"735","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from one hole twice."
"736","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shubah informed us, from Jabir, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not add in travel beyond two rakahs except to offer tahajjud at night; and Ibn Umar would not add beyond two rakahs. Jabir said: I said to Salim: Did they both offer witr? He said: Yes."
"737","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its soundness is evident."
"738","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me, a house in the Fire is built for him."
"739","Abu Asim narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed tribulation rises from here, from the east, from where the two horns of Satan rise."
"740","Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Asim ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: Umar sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Umrah, and he permitted him, and said to him: O my brother, do not forget us in your supplication. Umar said: It is dearer to me than the world."
"741","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by which he used to swear was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"742","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Hamzah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, who said: Abdullah ibn Umar informed me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will fold the heavens on the Day of Resurrection, then take them in His right hand, then say: I am the King, where are the tyrants, where are the arrogant? Then He will fold the earths, then take them in His left, then say: I am the King, where are the tyrants, where are the arrogant?"
"743","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he obligated the charity of Fitr saying: A sa of dates or a sa of barley. He said: Ibn Umar would only give dates, but his dates ran out one year, so he gave a sa of barley in place of dates."
"744","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: Whenever there was a rainy night on a journey, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would lead us in Maghrib prayer, then we would return to our mounts; and when his caller gave the call for the latter Isha, he would cry out at the end of his call when finished: O people, there is no congregation, so pray in your mounts."
"745","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock: the man is over the people of his house, the woman is over her house, the slave is over the wealth of his master, and the imam is a shepherd over the people; so each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock."
"746","Yala and Muhammad, sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale involving uncertainty; and that is because the people of ignorance used to engage in that sale: a man would buy the unborn offspring of an unborn camel for a decrepit she-camel, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that."
"747","And with his chain, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes in his sitting place on Friday, let him move to another place."
"748","Yala and Muhammad, sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, who said: Whenever the journey pressed Ibn Umar, he would delay Maghrib until the twilight disappeared, then alight and combine it with the latter Isha, saying: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing when the journey pressed him."
"749","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever deliberately leaves Asr until the sun sets, it is as if his family and wealth were taken away."
"750","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us sleep while in a state of major impurity? He said: Yes, and let him perform his ablution for prayer except for his feet. He said: Whenever Ibn Umar wanted to sleep or eat while in a state of major impurity, he would wash his private part, his palms, his face, and his hands."
"751","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mujabbar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek good with those of handsome faces."
"752","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hearing and obeying is binding upon the Muslim man in what he loves and hates, so long as he is not commanded with disobedience; whoever is commanded with disobedience, there is no hearing nor obedience for him."
"753","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is before you a Pond as wide as between Jarba or Harba and Adhruh."
"754","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gathers the first and the last for the Day of Resurrection, a banner is raised for every treacherous one, and it is said: This is the treachery of so-and-so, son of so-and-so."
"755","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced uninterrupted fasting in Ramadan, and his companions did likewise, so he forbade them. It was said to him: You practice uninterrupted fasting. He said: I am not like you; I am fed and given drink."
"756","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should propose over the proposal of his brother, nor sell over the sale of his brother, except with his permission."
"757","Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Judani narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn Hafs, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early morning."
"758","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Nafi ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nuaym narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Almighty has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart."
"759","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, strengthen Islam with the one of these two men more beloved to You: Umar ibn al-Khattab or Abu Jahl ibn Hisham. He said: The more beloved of the two to Him was Umar."
"760","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Awn al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the Stone and touched it, then placed his lips upon it weeping for a long time. I turned and there was Umar weeping, so he said: O Umar, here tears are shed."
"761","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad al-Zuhri narrated to me, from his father, from Salih ibn Kaysan: Nafi narrated to us, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Almighty will admit the people of Paradise into Paradise and admit the people of the Fire into the Fire, then a caller will stand between them and say: O people of Paradise, no death; and O people of the Fire, no death; each abiding forever in what he is in."
"762","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to me, who said: My father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, who said: Nafi narrated to us that Abdullah informed him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon the people of the well at Badr, then called to them and said: O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? Some of his companions said: O Messenger of Allah, do you call to dead people? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You do not hear what I say better than they do."
"763","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, who said: Nafi narrated to us, that Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will stand before the Lord of the worlds on the Day of Resurrection until one of them disappears up to the middle of his ears in his sweat."
"764","Said ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar al-Umari, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should make a man stand and then sit in his place; rather make room and widen. And whenever a man stood for Ibn Umar from his place, he would not sit in it."
"765","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayrah, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying in seven places: the rubbish heap, the slaughterhouse, the graveyard, the middle of the road, the bathhouse, the resting places of camels, and above the back of the House of Allah the Almighty."
"766","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not travel with the Quran, for I do not feel safe for it from the enemy."
"767","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his caller on a rainy night of cold and wind on a journey to proclaim: Pray in your mounts."
"768","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Hafs ibn Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not travel with the Quran to the land of the enemy, for I fear that they may get hold of something of it."
"769","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Nafi, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: You looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these eyes of yours? He said: Yes. He said: And you spoke to him with these tongues of yours and pledged to him with these hands of yours? He said: Yes. The man said: Glad tidings to you. Ibn Umar said: Shall I not inform you of what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying? He said: Yes. He said: I heard him saying: Glad tidings for whoever saw me and believed in me, twice; and glad tidings for whoever did not see me and believed in me, three times."
"770","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine in this world and then does not repent from it will be deprived of it in the Hereafter and will not be given it to drink."
"771","Ubaydullah informed us, from Mubarak ibn Hassan, from Nafi, who said: Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Almighty says: O son of Adam, two things were never yours, one of them: I have made for you a share in your wealth when I take you by your throat, to purify and cleanse you thereby, and the prayer of My servants upon you after your term ends."
"772","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head in the Farewell Hajj."
"773","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of you and the parable of the people of the two Books before you is like a man who hired laborers and said: Who will work from morning until midday for a qirat? So the Jews worked. Then he said: Who will work for me from midday until Asr prayer for a qirat? So the Christians worked. Then he said: Who will work for me from Asr prayer until the sun sets for two qirats? So you worked. The Jews and Christians became angry and said: Why do we have more work and less reward? He said: Have I decreased anything of your right? They said: No. He said: It is My bounty; I give it to whomever I will."
"774","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabanah. Ibn Umar said: Muzabanah is that a man sells the fruit of his land for a measured amount: if it increases it is his, and if it decreases it is upon him."
"775","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, who said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The upper hand is better than the lower hand; the upper hand is the giving hand, and the lower hand is the begging hand."
"776","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived on the Day of the Conquest and alighted in the courtyard of the Kabah, and sent to Uthman ibn Talhah, who came with the key. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House with Uthman ibn Talhah, Usamah, and Bilal. When they came out, the people hastened to them, so I said to Bilal: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray inside the House? He said: Yes. I said: Where? He said: Between the two front pillars, facing its front."
"777","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Respond to the invitation when you are invited."
"778","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your term among the terms of the nations before you is only like the time between Asr prayer and sunset."
"779","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami informed us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah and Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears and says: If Allah wills, has made an exception."
"780","Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to me, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that Zakat al-Fitr be paid before the people go out to the prayer."
"781","Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he would not pray the two rakahs after Maghrib nor after Jumuah except among his family."
"782","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: Bilal gave the call before the rising of Fajr, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to return and proclaim: Indeed the servant slept. So he returned and proclaimed: Indeed the servant slept, indeed the servant slept."
"783","Ahmad ibn Yunus informed me, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Jazari, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of my companions is like the stars, by which guidance is sought; whichever of them you take his word from, you will be guided."
"784","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Fatimah and found a curtain upon her door, so he did not enter upon her. He said: Rarely would he enter except with her permission. Ali came and saw her grieved, and said: What is wrong with you? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and did not enter upon me. Ali went to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah took it hard that you came to her and did not enter upon her. He said: What have I to do with the world, and what have I to do with figured designs? He said: He went to Fatimah and informed her of the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Then say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you command me? He said: Say to her: Let her send it to the sons of so-and-so."
"785","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would eat while walking and drink while standing."
"786","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: We would count for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a sitting: My Lord, forgive me and turn to me; indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Forgiving, a hundred times."
"787","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, who said: Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to me, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Nafi, freedman of Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Allah sent Adam down to the earth, the angels said: O Lord, will You place therein one who corrupts therein and sheds blood, while we glorify with Your praise and sanctify You? He said: I know what you do not know. They said: Our Lord, we are more obedient to You than the children of Adam. Allah said to the angels: Bring forward two angels from among the angels so that We may send them down to the earth. He said: Al-Zuharah appeared to them as a woman of the most beautiful of humans, and she came to them, and they asked her for herself. She said: No, by Allah, until you speak this word of polytheism. They said: No, by Allah, we will never associate anything with Allah. She went away from them, then returned carrying an infant boy, and they asked her for herself. She said: No, by Allah, until you kill this boy. They said: No, by Allah, we will never kill him. She went away, then returned carrying a cup of wine, and they asked her for herself. She said: No, by Allah, until you drink this wine. They drank and became intoxicated, and fell upon her and killed the boy. When they awoke, the woman said: By Allah, you have left nothing that you refused me except that you did it when you became intoxicated. They were then given a choice between the punishment of this world and the Hereafter, and they chose the punishment of this world."
"788","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah said: The food of one suffices two, the food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."
"789","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, al-Hakam ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat. It was said: You neither fed it nor gave it drink, nor did you let it go to eat from the vermin of the earth."
"790","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari informed us, that Abdullah ibn Dinar informed him, from Abdullah ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Quba riding and walking."
"791","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Zubayri Abu Ahmad informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are known to none but Allah the Almighty: none knows the Hour but Allah, none knows when the rain falls but Allah, none knows what is in the wombs but Allah, no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow but Allah, and no soul knows in which land it will die but Allah."
"792","Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among trees there is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is like the Muslim man. He said: The people fell into the trees of the deserts, and I was among the youngest of the people, and it occurred to my heart that it is the palm tree. He said: I mentioned that to my father, and he said: Had you said it, it would have been dearer to me than such and such."
"793","Said ibn Amir narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek it, or he said: Whoever seeks it, let him seek it on the night of the twenty-seventh."
"794","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, who said: Abu Uthman al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid informed me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most dutiful of dutifulness is that a man maintain ties with the beloved ones of his father."
"795","Abu Asim informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf on the Day of the Conquest upon his mount, touching the corners with his staff; and when he came out he found no place to alight, so he alighted upon the hands of men. Then he stood and addressed them, praising Allah and extolling Him, and said: Praise be to Allah who has removed from you the pride of ignorance and its boasting about forefathers. People are two men: a righteous, God-fearing one, noble before Allah the Almighty, and a wicked, wretched one, lowly before Allah the Almighty. Then he recited: O people, indeed We created you from male and female. Then he said: I say this and I seek forgiveness from Allah for me and for you."
"796","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing dogs, so they were killed, until they reached a woman at al-Aqabah and wanted to kill a dog. She said: I am at this place and it comforts me. They felt pity for her, so they returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he commanded them to kill it, so they killed it."
"797","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The poor among the Muslims complained of the preference given to their rich over them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, these brothers of ours believed as we believed, prayed as we prayed, and fasted as we fasted; they have preference over us in wealth: they give charity and maintain kinship, while we are poor and cannot do that. He said: Shall I not inform you of something which, if you do it, you will attain the like of their merit? Say after every prayer: Allah is Most Great eleven times, praise be to Allah eleven times, glory be to Allah eleven times, and there is no god but Allah alone without partner eleven times, and glory be to Allah eleven times, and there is no god but Allah alone without partner eleven times - you will attain the like of their merit. That reached the rich, and they said the like of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them. They came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, our brothers say the like of what we say. He said: That is the bounty of Allah; He gives it to whomever He wills. Shall I not give you glad tidings, O company of the poor: The poor among the believers will enter Paradise before their rich by half a day, five hundred years."
"798","Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: When the people alighted at al-Hijr in the expedition of Tabuk, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not enter upon these punished people - meaning the people of Salih - unless you are weeping; and if you are not weeping, do not enter, lest what befell them befall you."
"799","Dawud ibn Muhabbar narrated to me, Sukayn ibn Abi Siraj narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Dinar say: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil character spoils deeds just as vinegar spoils honey."
"800","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Said ibn Jubayr, who said: I saw Ibn Umar walking between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then he said: If I walked, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking, and if I hastened, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastening."
"801","Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi informed us, from Abu Hashim, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, who said: I believe it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: For a woman, from her pregnancy to her delivery to her weaning, there is reward like that of one striving hard in the path of Allah, and if she dies in between, she has the reward of a martyr."
"802","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Marzuq Abu Bakr informed us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which people recite best? He said: The one when you hear his recitation you see that he fears Allah, mighty and majestic."
"803","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The measure is the measure of the people of Medina, and the weight is the weight of the people of Mecca."
"804","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Shuayb, who said: I heard Tawus saying: Ibn Umar was asked about the two rakahs before Maghrib, and he said: I never saw anyone praying them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"805","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Grant your women permission at night to go to the mosques."
"806","Amr ibn Awn informed me, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks refuge with you in Allah, grant him refuge; whoever asks you in Allah, give him; whoever invites you, accept his invitation; and whoever does you a kindness, repay him, and if you find nothing, supplicate for him until you know that you have repaid him."
"807","Amr ibn Awn informed me, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days greater in the sight of Allah, nor more beloved to Him for deeds to be done therein, than these days, the ten of Dhu al-Hijjah - or he said: the ten - so increase therein in glorification, declaring there is no god but Allah, magnifying Allah, and praising Him."
"808","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Imran ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Qattat narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The people of the Fire will be made enormous until what is between the earlobe of one of them and his shoulder is a journey of seven hundred years, the thickness of his skin is forty cubits, and his molar tooth is greater than Mount Uhud."
"809","Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: He was asked how many times the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah, and he said: Twice. Then Aisha said: Ibn Umar knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah three times, besides the Umrah he joined with the Farewell Hajj."
"810","Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I heard him saying: I seek Allah's forgiveness, a hundred times: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and accept my repentance; indeed You are the Most Relenting, the Most Forgiving - or: indeed You are Relenting, Forgiving - the doubt is from Zuhayr."
"811","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Said al-Sammak informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, who said: One day Bilal was late with the call to prayer, so a man called the adhan; then Bilal came and wanted to call the iqamah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who called the adhan should call the iqamah."
"812","Abu Ishaq Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah: A man praised a man in the presence of Ibn Umar, so Ibn Umar began throwing dust toward his mouth, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see those who lavish praise, throw dust in their mouths - or he said: some dust."
"813","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Qutbah, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the husband's right over the wife? He said: She must not withhold herself from him even if she is on the back of a camel saddle. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the husband's right over the wife? He said: She must not give charity from his house in anything except with his permission; if she does, he gets the reward and upon her is the sin. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the husband's right over the wife? He said: She must not fast a day except with his permission; if she does, she sins and gets no reward. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the husband's right over the wife? He said: She must not leave his house except with his permission; if she does, the angels of Allah, the angels of mercy, and the angels of wrath curse her until she returns."
"814","Husayn al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O people, fear wrongdoing, for it will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"815","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in the grave, say: In the name of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah. Abd ibn Humayd said: Yazid said: No one raised this hadith as a Prophetic report except Hammam."
"816","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Abu al-Atuf al-Jarrah ibn Minhal al-Jazari informed us, from al-Zuhri, from a man, from Ibn Umar, who said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he entered one of the gardens of the Ansar, and he began picking dates and eating. He said to me: O Ibn Umar, why do you not eat? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no appetite for it. He said: But I do desire it, and this is the fourth morning in which I have not tasted food nor found it. If I wished, I could call upon my Lord and He would grant me the like of the kingdom of Khosrow and Caesar. How will it be with you, O Ibn Umar, when you remain among a people who hoard a year's provision, with weakened certainty. By Allah, we had not moved nor departed before there was revealed: And how many a creature does not carry its provision; Allah provides for it and for you, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has not commanded me to hoard the world, nor to follow desires. Whoever hoards worldly wealth seeking thereby an everlasting life, then life is in Allah's hand. Indeed, I do not hoard a dinar nor a dirham, nor do I store provision for tomorrow."
"817","Abu Usamah informed us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir al-Madani, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about water visited by wild beasts and animals, and he said: When water is two qullahs, it does not carry filth. Abu Usamah said: A qullah holds about the amount of a large waterskin."
"818","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn al-Mundhir, who said: I entered a garden of ours, its beginning, with Ubayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, and in it was a watering trough, and the trough was of camel hide, so he performed ablution. I said: You perform ablution while in it is camel hide? He said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When water reaches two qullahs, or three, it does not become impure."
"819","Shababah ibn Sawwar informed me, Israil ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in station is one who looks at his gardens, his wives, his bliss, his servants, and his couches over a journey of a thousand years; and the most honored of them in the sight of Allah, mighty and majestic, is one who looks at His Face morning and evening. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Faces on that Day will be radiant, looking toward their Lord."
"820","Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami Abu Hafs narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of dead animals and two kinds of blood have been made lawful for us: as for the two dead, the fish and the locust; and as for the two bloods, the liver and the spleen."
"821","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Hani, from Abbas al-Hajari, from Ibn Umar: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my servant misbehaves and wrongs; shall I strike him? He said: No, pardon him seventy times every day."
"822","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Yannaq, who said: I was with Ibn Umar in a mosque in Mecca when a young man passed with his lower garment trailing, so he said: O young man, from whom are you? He said: From Banu Bakr. He said: Would you not like Allah to look at you on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Glory be to Allah, yes indeed. He said: Then lift your garment, for I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two ears of mine - and he pointed with his fingers to his ears - saying: Whoever drags his garment seeking only pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"823","Yala narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"824","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in being alone, no one would ever travel alone at night."
"825","Yala narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Abu Dihqanah, from Ibn Umar, who said: There were people with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called Bilal for some dates he had, so he brought dates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapproved of. He said: What are these dates? He said: The dates we had, we exchanged two sas for one sa. He said: Give us back our dates."
"826","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wants his supplication to be answered and his distress to be relieved, let him relieve one in difficulty."
"827","Abd ibn Humayd informed us, from a shaykh of his, he said: Jafar ibn Burqan informed us, he said: Isa ibn Hafs ibn Asim ibn Umar informed us, from his father, who said: I was with Ibn Umar on a journey, and he led us in two rakahs, then departed and came to the cushion of his saddle and reclined on it, and he saw people standing behind him. He said: What are these people doing? I said: They are performing voluntary prayers. He said: If I were to perform voluntary prayers I would have completed my prayer; O son of my brother, I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until Allah took him, and he never exceeded two rakahs, two rakahs; then I accompanied Abu Bakr and he never exceeded two rakahs, two rakahs; then I accompanied Umar and he never exceeded two rakahs, two rakahs; then I accompanied Uthman and he never exceeded two rakahs, two rakahs. Then he recited: You certainly have in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"828","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim, the brother of al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging will persist with one of you until he meets Allah, mighty and majestic, with not a shred of flesh on his face."
"829","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Mawraq al-Ijli, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about prayer while traveling, and he said: Two rakahs, two rakahs; whoever contradicts the Sunnah has disbelieved."
"830","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Muttalib, who said: He invited a Bedouin to his food, that being a day after the slaughter day, and the Bedouin said: I am fasting. He said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding fasting these three days, meaning the days of Tashriq."
"831","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar and al-Thawri informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Wiping the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner in a crowd effaces sins completely."
"832","Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, who said: I saw Ibn Umar crowding at the Corner and the Yemeni Corner in a way I never saw any of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing, so I mentioned it to him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Touching them both is an expiation for sins. And I heard him saying: Whoever circumambulates the House seven times and completes it, it is equal to freeing a slave. He said: And I heard him saying: The pilgrim does not lift one foot nor place the other except that a good deed is written for him, a sin is effaced from him, and a rank is raised for him."
"833","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ali ibn Abdullah al-Bariqi, from Ibn Umar: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and mounted his camel, he would say Allahu Akbar three times, then say: Glory be to Him who has subjected this for us though we could not have subdued it, and indeed to our Lord we shall return. Then he would say: O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine righteousness and piety, and of deeds what pleases You. O Allah, ease the journey for us and fold up for us the distance of the land. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Guardian over the family. O Allah, accompany us in this journey of ours and watch over our families for us. And when he returned, he would say: Returning, if Allah wills, worshipping, repenting, praising our Lord."
"834","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ismail ibn Jarir, from Qazah, who said: Ibn Umar sent me on an errand and took my hand, and said: Come, let me bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade me farewell when he sent me on an errand of his. He said: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts, and the outcomes of your deeds."
"835","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: I had a wife whom I loved, and my father disliked her, so he ordered me to divorce her but I refused. So he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he sent for me and said: O Abdullah, divorce your wife. So I divorced her."
"836","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Ibn Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until the blight is gone. Ibn Suraqah said: I asked Ibn Umar what that meant, and he said: The rising of the Pleiades."
"837","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to me that he was sitting with Ibn Umar, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in his supplication in the evening and the morning, never abandoning it until he left this world and died: O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my worldly life, my family, and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and secure my fears. O Allah, protect me from before me, from behind me, from my right, from my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being swallowed up from beneath me. Jubayr said: That is being swallowed by the earth. Ubadah said: I do not know whether it is the saying of the Prophet or the saying of Jubayr."
"838","Abu Nuaym informed us, Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad narrated to me, he said: We went out with Ibn Umar on the day of Adha or Fitr, and he walked until he came to the prayer ground, then sat until the imam came, then prayed and departed. Then Ibn Umar departed and did not pray any prayer before it nor after it. I said: O Ibn Umar, there is no prayer before it nor after it? He said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing."
"839","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the witr prayer upon his camel."
"840","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, that he used to like yellow color even in the turban, and claimed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like yellow color."
"841","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Tumah narrated to us, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I am able to fast while traveling. Ibn Umar said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever does not accept Allah's concession, upon him will be sin like the mountains of Arafah."
"842","Al-Walid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Walid al-Hamdani narrated to me, al-Sabbah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abu Dawud al-Subayi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No one will remain on the day of Arafah with faith weighing a speck in his heart except that he will be forgiven. A man said: Is this only for those at Arafah, O Messenger of Allah, or for people in general? He said: Rather, for people in general."
"843","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Abu Shubah al-Hanafi narrated to me, he said: al-Rabi or Abu al-Rabi al-Hanzali narrated to me, he said: I prayed with Ibn Umar and said to him: Sometimes you lead us in prayer and I cannot discern my companion's face when you give the salam, and sometimes you pray and when you give the salam I see that the sun has risen. He said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying, and I love to pray as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying."
"844","Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah: Hafs ibn Asim saw him performing voluntary prayers while traveling, and with them on that journey was Abdullah ibn Umar. Hafs said: A brother of yours forbids this, meaning Ibn Umar. So I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: I saw the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not doing that while traveling; he would not perform voluntary prayers before the prayer nor after it. He said: I said: Shall I pray at night? He said: Yes, pray at night as much as you wish upon your mount, wherever it turns with you."
"845","Said ibn Sallam narrated to me, Zakariya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while upon the pulpit addressing the people, saying: You will not come to Allah on the Day of Resurrection with anything better than your prayer. Indeed, the night prayer is two by two; then when you fear the dawn, pray one."
"846","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to me, Qatadah narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini, who said: I was holding Ibn Umar's hand when a man came to him and said: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speaking about the private conversation on the Day of Resurrection? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, mighty and majestic, will draw the believer near until He places His covering over him and shields him from the people. He will say: Do you recognize such-and-such sin? He will say: Yes, my Lord. He will say: Do you recognize such-and-such sin? He will say: Yes, my Lord. He will say: Do you recognize such-and-such sin? He will say: Yes, my Lord. Until, when He has made him confess his sins and he thinks in himself that he is ruined, He will say: I have forgiven them for you today. Then he will be given his record of good deeds. As for the disbelievers and hypocrites, the witnesses will say: These are those who lied against their Lord; indeed, the curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers."
"847","Sulayman ibn Dawud and Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from his father, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he has not reached the death rattle."
"848","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, he said: Hassan ibn Atiyah narrated to me, from Abu Munib al-Jurashi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent before the Hour with the sword, my provision was placed in the shade of my spear, and humiliation and disgrace were placed upon whoever opposes my command. Whoever imitates a people is one of them."
"849","Al-Aswad ibn Amir informed us, Baqiyyah al-Himsi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Zufar, from Hashim, from Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever buys a garment for ten dirhams with a haram dirham in it, no prayer of his will be accepted so long as it is upon him. Then he put his two fingers in his ears and said: May they both be deaf if I did not hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it."
"850","Umar ibn Sad al-Hafari narrated to us, from Badr ibn Uthman, from Ubaydullah ibn Marwan, Abu Aishah narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one morning and said: Before the dawn prayer I saw as though I was given the keys and the balances. As for the keys, these are the keys, and as for the balances, these are what are weighed with. I was placed in one pan and my nation was placed in the other, and I outweighed them. Then Abu Bakr was brought and weighed, and he outweighed them. Then Umar was brought and weighed, and he outweighed them. Then Uthman was brought and weighed, and he outweighed them. Then I awoke and it was lifted."
"851","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Shihab narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Dinar al-Nili informed me, from Hammad ibn Jafar, from Ibn Umar, who said: Shall I not inform you of the lowest of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes indeed. He said: A man who enters through the gate of Paradise and his servants meet him, saying to him: Welcome to you, our master; the time has come for you to return. He said: Carpets are spread for him for forty years, then he looks to his right and left and sees the gardens, and says: To whom does all this belong? It will be said: To you. Until, when he finishes, a red ruby or a green emerald is raised for him, having seventy branches, in each branch seventy rooms, in each room seventy doors. It will be said to him: Recite and ascend. So he ascends until, when he reaches the throne of his kingdom, he reclines upon it, its expanse a mile by a mile, with surplus beyond it. Seventy thousand plates of gold are brought to him, no plate among them having the same dish as its companion; he finds the pleasure of the last of it as he finds the pleasure of the first of it. Then various drinks are brought to him and he drinks whatever he desires. Then the servants say: Leave him with his wives. Abu Shihab said: And I think he said: So he withdraws from the servants, and behold, one of the wide-eyed houris is sitting upon the throne of her kingdom; he sees the marrow of her shins through the clarity of flesh and blood. He says to her: Who are you? She says: I am one of the wide-eyed houris kept for you. He looks at her for forty years without lifting his gaze from her. Then he raises his gaze to the chambers above him and sees another more beautiful than her, and she says: Has not the time come for us to have a share of you? So he ascends to her and looks at her for forty years without turning his gaze from her. Until, when bliss has reached them in every measure and they think there is no bliss better than it, the Lord, blessed and exalted, manifests Himself to them and they look at the Face of the Most Merciful, mighty and majestic, and they forget every bliss they witnessed when they looked at the Face of the Most Merciful, mighty and majestic. He says: O people of Paradise, declare My oneness. So they respond with the declaration of oneness. He says: O Dawud, stand and glorify Me as you used to glorify Me in the world. So Dawud glorifies his Lord, mighty and majestic. Ahmad ibn Yunus said: I said to Abu Shihab: The hadith of Khalid ibn Dinar about the mention of Paradise, did he raise it as a Prophetic report? He said: Yes."
"852","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Qays narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Abi Thabit, from Tamim ibn Iyad, from Ibn Umar, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taking the pre-dawn meal, when he finished his meal, Alqamah ibn Ulathah came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited him to a head of meat. While he was eating, Bilal came to announce the prayer to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Bilal, until Alqamah finishes his meal."
"853","Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi narrated to me, Mindal ibn Ali al-Anazi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Nimah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever witnesses the wedding feast of a Muslim, it is as though he fasted a day in the path of Allah, and a day is like seven hundred days. Whoever witnesses the funeral of a Muslim, it is as though he fasted a day in the path of Allah, and a day is like seven hundred days. Whoever visits a sick person, it is as though he fasted a day in the path of Allah, and a day is like seven hundred days. Whoever prays over a funeral, it is as though he fasted a day in the path of Allah, and a day is like seven hundred days. And whoever bathes on Friday, it is as though he fasted a day in the path of Allah, and a day is like seven hundred days."
"854","Malik ibn Ismail narrated to me, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Abi Jafar al-Ashjai, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led his companions in the dawn prayer while traveling and recited: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, the One. And he said: I have recited for you a third of the Quran and a quarter of it."
"855","Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Nahshal al-Dabbi, from Abu Ghalib, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Luqman the Wise used to say: When something is entrusted to Allah, mighty and majestic, He preserves it."
"856","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Kunasah al-Asadi narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Said ibn Amr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains within the latitude of his religion so long as he does not shed unlawful blood."
"857","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Did you do such-and-such? He said: No, by the One besides whom there is no god. Then Jibril came to him and said: Yes indeed, he did it, but he was forgiven for his saying: There is no god but Allah."
"858","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Zayd ibn Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar: This surah was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the middle of the days of Tashriq at Mina during the Farewell Hajj: When the help of Allah and the victory comes, until its end. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew it meant farewell, so he ordered his she-camel al-Qaswa and she was saddled for him; he mounted and stood before the people at al-Aqabah, and the people gathered to him. He praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: O people, every bloodshed of the pre-Islamic age is annulled, and the first of your blood I annul is the blood of Iyas ibn Rabiah ibn al-Harith, who was nursed among Banu Layth and Hudhayl killed him. The first usury of the pre-Islamic age is the usury of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib; it is waived for you: your capital sums, you shall neither wrong nor be wronged. O people, time has turned and is today as it was on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. The number of months in the sight of Allah is twelve months in the Book of Allah, of them four are sacred: Rajab of Mudar between Jumada and Shaban, Dhu al-Qadah, Dhu al-Hijjah, and al-Muharram. Postponement of sacred months is an increase in disbelief by which those who disbelieve are led astray; they declare it lawful one year and forbidden one year to conform to the number Allah has made sacred. That is because they used to make Safar unlawful one year and lawful one year, and make al-Muharram lawful one year and unlawful one year, and that postponement is from Satan. O people, Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of yours at the end of time, but is content with despised deeds from you, so beware of him in your religion. O people, whoever has a trust, let him return it to the one who entrusted him. O people, women are captives with you; you took them by Allah's trust and made their private parts lawful by Allah's word. You have rights over them and they have rights over you. Of your rights is that they not allow your beds to be trodden upon, nor disobey you in what is right. If they do that, they have their provision and clothing in a fitting manner. If you strike, strike without severity. O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah. O people, what day is this? They said: A sacred day. He said: What month is this? They said: A sacred month. He said: What land is this? They said: A sacred land. He said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has made your blood, your wealth, and your honor sacred like the sacredness of this day and this month. There is no prophet after me, nor any nation after you. Let your present convey to your absent. Then he raised his hands and said: O Allah, bear witness that I have conveyed - three times."
"859","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Ifriqi, from Abu Ghutayf, from Ibn Umar: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution while already in a state of purity, ten good deeds are written for him."
"860","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Yazid al-Thumali, Abu Ajlan al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The disbeliever will drag his tongue on the Day of Resurrection behind him for two farsakhs, with people trampling upon it."
"861","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No people gather remembering Allah, mighty and majestic, except that the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him. And he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, grants respite until, when it is the last third of the night, He descends to this heaven and calls out: Is there any sinner repenting? Is there anyone seeking forgiveness? Is there anyone supplicating? Is there anyone asking? Until dawn."
"862","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sulayman ibn Ali al-Rabai informed us, Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, like for like, hand to hand; wheat for wheat, like for like, hand to hand; silver for silver, like for like, hand to hand; dates for dates, like for like, hand to hand; barley for barley, like for like, hand to hand; salt for salt, like for like, hand to hand. Whoever gives more or asks for more has engaged in usury; the taker and giver are alike."
"863","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Abu Masud al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the Fire whom Allah does not intend to bring out neither die therein nor live. As for the people of the Fire whom Allah intends to bring out, He causes them to die therein a death until they become charcoal therein, then they come out in batches and are cast upon the rivers of Paradise; the water of the rivers of Paradise is sprinkled over them until they sprout as seeds sprout in the silt of a flood. The people of Paradise call them the Jahannamis. Then they ask Allah to remove that name from them, and He removes it from them."
"864","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us after Asr until the sun was about to set. Those of us who memorized it memorized it, and those who forgot it forgot it. He said: Indeed, the world is green and sweet, and Allah will make you successors in it and see how you act. Beware of the world and beware of women. The children of Adam were created upon various levels: among them is one born a believer, living a believer, and dying a believer; among them is one born a believer, living a believer, and dying a disbeliever; among them is one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, and dying a disbeliever; and among them is one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, and dying a believer. Anger is a live coal kindled in the heart of the son of Adam; do you not see the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his jugular veins? Whoever finds anything of that, let him cleave to the ground. The best of men is one slow to anger and quick to return; if he is quick to anger and quick to return, it balances out. The worst of men is one quick to anger and slow to return; if he is quick to anger and quick to return, it balances out. The best of traders is one good in seeking payment and good in paying; the worst of traders is one bad in seeking and bad in paying; if he is good in seeking and bad in paying, or bad in seeking and good in paying, it balances out. Every treacherous person will have a banner by which he is known on the Day of Resurrection. No excuse is greater than the excuse of a ruler over the generality. The best jihad is a word of justice before an unjust ruler. Let not fear of people prevent anyone from speaking the truth when he witnesses it or knows it. Until, when it was near sunset, he said: What remains of the world compared to what has passed of it is only like what remains of this sun until it sets."
"865","Safwan ibn Isa informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the people of the Fire who are its permanent inhabitants, they neither live therein nor die - or: they neither die therein nor live. As for people whom Allah, mighty and majestic, intends mercy for, the Fire causes them to die, then the intercessors come to them and carry bundles of them and scatter them upon a river in Paradise, a river called the River of Life, or the River of Modesty, or the River of Vitality. They sprout as seeds sprout in the silt of a flood. Have you not seen a tree, at times green, then yellow, or yellow, then green? A man among the people said: It is as though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the desert."
"866","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Iyas, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us as a detachment of thirty men. We alighted by a people at night and they refused to host us, so we alighted aside. Their chief was stung, so they came to us and said: Is there anyone among you who performs ruqya? We said: Yes. They said: Come along. We said: Not unless you give us a wage, for you refused to host us. So they gave us thirty sheep. I went with them and began reciting the Opening of the Book and wiping the place that was stung until he recovered, so they gave us the sheep. I said: By Allah, we shall not eat them until we ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them, for I do not know what ruqya is nor am I skilled in ruqya. When we came, we went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: And how did you know it is a ruqya, and how did you know it is a ruqya? Yes, eat them, and allot a share for me with you."
"867","Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shubah informed us, Abu Maslamah informed us, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah say: Abu Said said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is green and sweet, and Allah is making you successors in it and seeing how you act. So beware the trial of the world and the trial of women. The first trial of the Children of Israel was concerning women."
"868","Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Maslamah, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the Fire who are its permanent inhabitants neither die therein nor live. But it afflicts peoples for their sins or their errors; when they become charcoal, permission is given for intercession, so they are brought out bundle by bundle and scattered upon the rivers of Paradise. A caller calls out: O people of Paradise, pour water upon them. So they sprout as seeds sprout in the silt of a flood."
"869","Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Maslamah, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or knows it. Abu Said said: That carried me to ride to Muawiyah and fill his ears, then I returned."
"870","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of hospitality is three days; what exceeds that is charity."
"871","Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh."
"872","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a man is confused in his prayer and does not know whether he added or omitted, let him prostrate twice while sitting."
"873","Ali ibn Asim informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah al-Abdi, he said: Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon leaning against a palm trunk. The people said to him: O Messenger of Allah, the people have increased, meaning the Muslims, and they love to see you; if only you would take a pulpit to stand upon so the people may see you. He said: Yes. Who will make this pulpit for us? A man stood up to him and said: I will make it. He said: Will you make it? He said: Yes, and he did not say: If Allah wills. He said: What is your name? He said: So-and-so. He said: Sit down. So he sat. Then he repeated: Who will make this pulpit for us? A man stood up to him and said: I will. He said: Will you make it? He said: Yes, and he did not say: If Allah wills. He said: What is your name? He said: So-and-so. He said: Sit down. Then he repeated: Who will make this pulpit for us? A man stood up to him and said: I will. He said: Will you make it? He said: Yes, if Allah wills. He said: What is your name? He said: Ibrahim. He said: Make it. When Friday came, the people gathered for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the end of the mosque. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and settled upon it, the palm trunk moaned until it made me hear, though I was at the end of the mosque. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended from the pulpit and embraced it, and did not cease until it calmed. Then he returned to the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: This palm trunk only moaned out of longing for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he left it. By Allah, had I not descended to it and embraced it, it would not have calmed until the Day of Resurrection."
"874","Abu Nuaym narrated to me, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lagging among his companions, so he said: Come forward and complete the prayer with me, and let those after you follow you. People will keep lagging until Allah, mighty and majestic, puts them behind."
"875","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man with two sandals of fire on his feet from which his brain boils; among them is one in the Fire up to his ankles along with the infliction of torment; among them is one in the Fire up to his knees along with the infliction of torment; among them is one in the Fire up to his groin along with the infliction of torment; among them is one in the Fire up to his chest along with the infliction of torment; and among them is one submerged in the Fire."
"876","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Ibn Said about the soil of Paradise, and he said: Fine white flour, pure musk. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"877","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Fadl narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: While a shepherd was grazing his sheep, a wolf came and took a sheep from them, so the shepherd came between it and the sheep. The wolf sat upon its tail and said: O shepherd, fear Allah; you come between me and provision that Allah has provided me. The shepherd said: Strange, a wolf sitting upon its tail speaking to me with human speech. The wolf said: Shall I not inform you of something stranger than that? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Harrah narrating to the people reports of what has passed. So the shepherd drove his sheep until he came to Medina and penned them aside, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and narrated to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You spoke the truth. Then he said: Among the signs of the Hour is that beasts will speak to humans. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the Hour will not come until a man's whip-handle speaks to him, and his sandal-strap, and his thigh informs him of what his family did."
"878","Abu al-Walid informed us, Hammam informed us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three gather, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the best reciter among them."
"879","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: Our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book and whatever is easy."
"880","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Naamah al-Sadi, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with his companions, he took off his sandals and placed them to his left. When the Muslims saw that, they cast off their sandals. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: What made you cast off your sandals? They said: We saw you cast off, so we cast off. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and informed me that there was filth or harm in them. When one of you comes to the mosque, let him look; if he sees filth in his sandal, let him wipe it, then pray in it."
"881","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, so Jibril, peace be upon him, performed ruqya for him and said: In the name of Allah I perform ruqya for you, from everything that harms you, from every envier and eye; Allah heals you."
"882","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a new garment, he would name it by its name - a shirt, a turban, or a cloak - saying: O Allah, praise belongs to You; You clothed me with it. I ask You for its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was made for."
"883","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) secluded himself in the mosque and heard them raising their voices in recitation while he was in his dome. He lifted the curtain and said: Each of you is conversing privately with his Lord, mighty and majestic, so let none of you harm another, nor let one raise his voice over another in the Quran - or he said: in prayer."
"884","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, he said: Said ibn Khalid al-Qarazi narrated to me, he said: I visited Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman at Quba, and Abu Salamah had married a woman from Banu Amr ibn Awf. He served me butter, and a fly fell into the butter, so Abu Salamah began scooping it with his little finger. I said: May Allah forgive you, O uncle. Abu Salamah said: I heard Abu Said saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a fly falls into food, immerse it, for in one of its wings is poison and in the other is cure; it presents the poison and delays the cure."
"885","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man sees the private part of his brother and covers it for him except that he will be admitted to Paradise."
"886","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Atiyah ibn Sad al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I enjoy comfort when the bearer of the Trumpet has seized the Trumpet, bent his forehead, and inclined his hearing, waiting until he is commanded? The Muslims said: What shall we say? He said: Say: Allah suffices us, and He is the best Guardian; upon Him we rely."
"887","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid and Salim al-Muradi narrated to us, from Atiyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as you see a star on the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent. Salim said: Meaning by his saying: and how excellent, they are raised high. Atiyah was a man inclined to Shiism."
"888","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Atiyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wealthy are ruined. They said: Except whom? He said: The wealthy are ruined. They said: Except whom? They said: Until we feared it had become binding. He said: Except one who says thus and thus, and few are they."
"889","Jafar ibn Awn informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Atiyah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights his brother, let him avoid the face."
"890","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Atiyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise."
"891","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Atiyah narrated to me, Abu Said narrated to me: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the forenoon prayer until we thought he would never leave it, and would leave it until we thought he would never pray it."
"892","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Atiyah, Abu Said narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will enter Paradise except by Allah's mercy. We said: O Messenger of Allah, not even you? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me - and he placed his hand upon his head - I think he said: with His mercy."
"893","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi narrated to us, he said: Atiyah narrated to me, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I attended a funeral at which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present. When it was placed down, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes. So he turned away from us and said: Pray over your companion. When Ali saw him turning away, he said: O Prophet of Allah, he is free of his sin; I guarantee what is upon him. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came forward and prayed over him, then departed and said: O Ali, may Allah and Islam reward you with good; may Allah release your pledge on the Day of Resurrection as you released your Muslim brother's pledge. There is no servant who settles his brother's debt except that Allah releases his pledge on the Day of Resurrection. A man of the Ansar stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for Ali specifically? He said: No, rather for the generality of Muslims."
"894","Abdullah ibn Musa informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is not grateful to people is not grateful to Allah."
"895","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Atiyah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich person except in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, or for the traveler, or when he has a poor neighbor who is given charity and then gifts to him from it."
"896","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Atiyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection and say: Today I am entrusted with every obstinate tyrant and whoever set up another god with Allah. It will fold over them and cast them into the depths of Hell."
"897","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Atiyah, from Abu Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet except that he warned his nation of the Dajjal, and I warn you of him. He is one-eyed, with a protruding pupil, unmistakable, like spittle on the side of a wall; his left eye is like a glittering star. With him is the like of Paradise and the like of Fire; his paradise is dusty with smoke, and his fire is a green garden. Before him are two men warning the people of the towns; whenever they leave a town, their vanguard enters it. He is given power over a man over none other, so he slaughters him, then strikes him with a staff, then says: Stand, and he stands. He says to his companions: What do you think? So they testify to him in polytheism. The slaughtered man says: O people, this is the false Messiah Dajjal whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us of; this has only increased me in insight about you. He returns and slaughters him, striking him with a staff he has, saying: Stand, and he stands. He says: What do you think? So they testify to him in polytheism. The slaughtered man says: O people, this is the false Messiah Dajjal whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us of; this has only increased me in insight about you. He returns and slaughters him, striking him with a staff he has, saying to him: Stand, and he stands. He says to his companions: What do you think? So they testify to him in polytheism. The slaughtered man says: O people, this is the Messiah whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us of; this has only increased me in insight about you. He returns a fourth time to slaughter him, but Allah places a plate of copper upon his throat, so he wants to slaughter him but cannot. Abu Said said: I did not know what copper was until that day. We thought that man was Umar ibn al-Khattab, until Umar ibn al-Khattab died. He said: And people plant and sow after that."
"898","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Atiyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The people of camels and the people of sheep boasted before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tranquility and dignity are among the people of sheep, and pride and arrogance are among the people of camels. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Musa was sent while grazing sheep for his family. He said: And I was sent while grazing sheep for my family at Ajyad."
"899","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Atiyah ibn Sad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or a man asked him - saying: O Messenger of Allah, a wolf cut off the tail of a sheep of mine; may I sacrifice it? He said: Yes."
"900","Ibrahim ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Atiyah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights his brother, let him avoid the face, for Allah, blessed and exalted, created Adam in His image."
"901","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever purifies himself and perfects purification, then comes to Friday without idle talk or ignorance, it is an expiation for what is between it and the next Friday. The five prayers are expiations for what is between them. On Friday there is an hour no Muslim servant coincides with asking Allah, mighty and majestic, for good therein except that He grants it to him."
"902","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyah, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: The day when some of your Lord's signs come, no soul's faith will benefit it. He said: The rising of the sun from its west."
"903","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, he said: Atiyah al-Awfi narrated to me that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has been given a gift to be fulfilled, and I have saved my gift as intercession for my nation."
"904","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, he said: Atiyah al-Awfi narrated to me that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have a Pool whose length is what is between the Kabah and Bayt al-Maqdis, white like milk. And I have the most followers among the prophets on the Day of Resurrection."
"905","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isa ibn Musa, from Atiyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, will bring out a people from the Fire after nothing remains of them therein except their faces, and admit them to Paradise."
"906","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from his father, who said: The first to bring out the pulpit on a festival day was Marwan, and he began with the sermon before the prayer. A man stood up to him and said: You opposed the Sunnah, O Marwan; you brought out the pulpit though it was never brought out, and you began with the sermon before the prayer. Abu Said said: Who is this? They said: This is so-and-so son of so-and-so. He said: As for this one, he has discharged what was upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever among you sees an evil, if he is able to change it with his hand; if unable, then with his tongue; if unable, then with his heart - and that is the weakest of faith."
"907","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Riyah ibn Ubaydah, from a man, from Abu Said, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate or drank, he would say: Praise belongs to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims."
"908","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and the Fire boasted. The Fire said: O my Lord, the tyrants, the arrogant, kings, and notables enter me. Paradise said: O my Lord, the weak, the poor, and the needy enter me. Allah, blessed and exalted, said: You are My punishment; I strike with you whom I will. And He said to Paradise: You are My mercy, encompassing all things. Each one will have its fill. The people of the Fire are cast into the Fire and it says: Is there more? He said: And they are cast therein and it says: Is there more? Until the Blessed and Exalted comes to it and places His foot upon it, and it contracts and says: Enough, enough. As for Paradise, there remains of it what Allah wills to remain, so Allah creates for it a creation as He wills."
"909","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from a son of Abu Said al-Khudri, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters with yawning."
"910","Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ablution for one who does not mention Allah's name, mighty and majestic."
"911","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Said informed us, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, raising the hadith, who said: There are three at whom Allah, mighty and majestic, laughs with pleasure: the man when he stands at night praying, the people when they line up in prayer, and the people when they line up facing the enemy."
"912","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and narrated to us what will be until the Day of Resurrection."
"913","Jafar ibn Awn informed us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nuh will be called and it will be said: Did you convey? He will say: Yes. Then his people will be called and it will be said: Did he convey to you? They will say: No warner came to us and no one came to us. Then He will say: Who are your witnesses? He will say: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his nation. Then you will be brought forth and you will bear witness that he conveyed, and that is the statement of Allah, Exalted and Mighty: And thus We have made you a just middle nation, and al-Wasat means the just, that you may be witnesses over people and the Messenger may be a witness over you."
"914","Yala informed us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hellfire enter Hellfire, death will be brought as though it were a black-and-white ram. A caller will call out: O people of Hellfire, do you recognize this? They will crane their necks and look, and all of them will have seen it. They will say: Yes, this is death. Then a caller will call out: O people of Paradise, do you recognize this? They will crane their necks and look, and all of them will have seen it. They will say: Yes, this is death. Then it will be seized and slaughtered. Then it will be said: O people of Paradise, eternity with no death, and O people of Hellfire, eternity with no death. That is His statement, Exalted and Mighty: And warn them of the Day of Regret when the matter is decided, while they are in heedlessness. He said: The people of this world are in heedlessness."
"915","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, who said: A group of the Ansar gathered and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has preferred others over us. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gathered them and addressed them, then said: O company of the Ansar, were you not humiliated and Allah honored you? They said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. He said: Were you not astray and Allah guided you through me? They said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. He said: Were you not poor and Allah enriched you through me? They said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Then he said: Will you not answer? Will you not say: You came to us driven away and we sheltered you, and you came to us fearful and we gave you security? Then he said: Are you not pleased that people should depart with sheep and camels while you depart with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), bringing him into your homes? If you were to take a valley or a mountain pass and the people took another valley or pass, I would take your valley or your pass. Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been one of the Ansar. You will encounter selfish preference after me, so be patient until you meet me."
"916","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil ibn Yunus informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a woman said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, set aside a day for us from yourself. He said: Yes, on such-and-such a day in such-and-such a place. So he came to them and taught them the Sunnah, and said: There is no woman who sends forth three children before her except that they will be a shield for her from the Fire. A woman said: Or two, O Messenger of Allah? He fell silent. Then she said: Or two, O Messenger of Allah? He fell silent. Then he said: Or two."
"917","Muhadir ibn al-Muwarra narrated to me, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, according to what he saw, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, will say on the Day of Resurrection: O Adam. He will say: At Your service and blessedness, and all good is in Your Hands. He will say: Send forth the contingent of Hellfire. He will say: O Lord, what is the contingent of Hellfire? He will say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine. At that point, the newborn will turn grey-haired, every pregnant female will drop her burden, and you will see people as though drunk though they are not drunk, but the punishment of Allah is severe. He said: That weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: O Messenger of Allah, which of us will be that one? He said: One man from among you, and a thousand from Yajuj and Majuj. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I hope that you will be a quarter of the people of Paradise. He said: So they said Allahu Akbar. Then he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I hope that you will be a third of the people of Paradise. He said: So they said Allahu Akbar. Then he said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. Then he said: You are among people only like a white hair on the hide of a black bull, or like a black hair on the hide of a white bull."
"918","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile my Companions. Leave my Companions for me, for if one of you were to spend gold equal to Uhud, he would not reach the mudd of one of them."
"919","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and he does not drink wine while he is a believer, yet repentance remains open."
"920","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord? He said: Do you suffer any harm in seeing the sun at midday when there are no clouds? We said: No. He said: Do you suffer any harm in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon when there are no clouds? We said: No. He said: Then you will suffer no harm in seeing Him except just as you suffer no harm in seeing them."
"921","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, says: Fasting is for Me and I shall reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast he rejoices, and when he meets Allah, Exalted and Mighty, he rejoices. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the changed smell of the fasting persons mouth is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"922","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh informed us, who said: Abu Hani al-Tujibi narrated to me, who said: I heard Abu Ali al-Tujibi that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are one hundred degrees in Paradise; between every two degrees is like what is between heaven and earth, or farther. I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, for whom are they? He said: For the mujahidin in the cause of Allah, Exalted and Mighty."
"923","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see a man frequenting the mosque, bear witness for him that he has faith, for Allah, Exalted and Mighty, said: Only those maintain the mosques of Allah who believe in Allah and the Last Day."
"924","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Wayl is a valley into which the disbeliever will fall for forty autumns before reaching its bottom, and al-Saud is a mountain of the fire of Hell which he will climb for seventy autumns, then he will fall down from it likewise, forever."
"925","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Remember Allah, Exalted and Mighty, abundantly, until it is said that he is mad."
"926","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The distance between the two leaves of a gate in Paradise is a journey of forty years."
"927","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truest dreams are those seen in the last part of the night before dawn."
"928","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, who said: Salim ibn Ghaylan informed me that he heard Darraj Abu al-Samh narrating from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Allah is pleased with a servant, He praises him with seven kinds of good that he did not do, and when He is displeased with a servant, He censures him with seven kinds of evil that he did not do."
"929","Abd Allah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, who said: I heard Darraj saying: I heard Abu al-Haytham saying: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ninety-nine dragons will be set upon the disbeliever in his grave, biting and stinging him until the Hour is established; if one of them were to breathe upon the earth, it would never again bring forth green growth."
"930","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Rishdin ibn Sad, who said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His statement, Exalted and Mighty: With water like molten metal: He said: Like the dregs of oil; when it is brought near to him, the skin of his face falls off into it."
"931","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to me, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to me, from Salim ibn Ghaylan, that he heard Darraj Abu al-Samh saying: He heard Abu al-Haytham saying: He heard Abu Said saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I seek refuge with Allah from disbelief and debt. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you equate disbelief with debt? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes."
"932","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Iblis said: O Lord, I will continue to lead the children of Adam astray so long as their souls are in their bodies. He said: Then the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: By My Might and Majesty, I will continue to forgive them so long as they seek My forgiveness."
"933","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from his father, that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the bier is placed down and men carry it on their necks, if it was righteous it says: Take me forward, and if it was not righteous it says: Woe to her, where are they taking her? Everything hears its voice except man, and if man were to hear it he would fall unconscious."
"934","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in the adhan, they would fight one another for it with swords."
"935","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Qatadah: Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers will be delivered from the Fire and detained at a bridge between Paradise and Hellfire, where retaliation will be exacted for some of them from others for wrongs that were between them in this world, until when they have been refined and cleansed, they will be granted permission to enter Paradise. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, one of them will be better guided to his dwelling in Paradise than he was to his dwelling in this world. He said: And some of them said: They resemble none but the people of Friday when they disperse from their Friday prayer. O Allah, make us among those granted permission to enter Paradise, O Most Kind, O Most Merciful. [Note: the closing supplication is part of the transmitted text.]"
"936","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Sulayman al-Naji, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said, who said: A man came after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already prayed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will trade profitably with this man? So a man stood and prayed with him."
"937","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Ali, who said: I heard Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji saying: Abu Said al-Khudri said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who supplicates with a supplication in which there is no sin nor severing of kinship ties, except that Allah gives him one of three things: either his supplication is hastened for him, or it is stored up for him in the Hereafter, or an equivalent amount of evil is averted from him. They said: Then we will supplicate abundantly. He said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, gives more and is more generous."
"938","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother is suffering from looseness of the bowels. He said: Give him honey to drink. So he gave him to drink. He said: Then he came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave him to drink and it only increased his looseness. He said: Give him honey to drink. So he gave him to drink. He said: Then he came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave him to drink and it only increased his looseness. He said: Give him honey to drink. So he gave him to drink, on the third or the fourth time, I think he said, then he was cured. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah spoke the truth and your brothers belly lied."
"939","Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: We asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a child is the delight of the eye and the perfection of joy, so will the people of Paradise have children? He said: When a man desires, or wishes, then within a single hour of the day will be what he wants of bearing, delivery, and youth."
"940","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Bishr al-Hujaymi, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Said, who said: We used to estimate the standing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr; we estimated his standing in Zuhr in the first two rakahs as about thirty verses, and we estimated his standing in the last two rakahs at half of that, and we estimated his standing in the first two rakahs of Asr as equal to the last two of Zuhr, and we estimated his standing in the last two of Asr at half of that."
"941","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will continue to perform Hajj and Umrah and plant date-palms after the emergence of Yajuj and Majuj."
"942","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from al-Thawri: Abu Ishaq informed us that al-Agharr narrated to him, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A caller will call out: It is for you to live and never die, it is for you to be healthy and never fall ill, it is for you to remain youthful and never grow old, and it is for you to enjoy bliss and never suffer misery. That is His statement, Exalted and Mighty: And they will be called: That is Paradise which you have been made to inherit for what you used to do."
"943","Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, that he bore witness against Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said that they both bore witness against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When the servant says: There is no god but Allah and Allah is Greatest, the Blessed and Exalted says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me and I am Alone. When he says: There is no god but Allah, Alone with no partner, He says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, with no partner. When he says: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, He says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, to Me belongs dominion and to Me belongs praise. When he says: There is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, He says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, and there is no power nor strength except through Me. Abu Ishaq said: Then al-Agharr said something I did not understand, so I said to Abu Jafar: What did he say? He said: He said: Whoever is granted these words at the time of his death, the Fire will not touch him."
"944","Musab ibn Miqdam al-Khathami narrated to us, Israil ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Muslim al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, that they both bore witness against the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and I bear witness through them against him — that they both narrated to him that he said: When the servant says: There is no god but Allah and Allah is Greatest, his Lord confirms him and says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me and I am Greatest. When he says: There is no god but Allah, Alone, his Lord confirms him and says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me and I am Alone. When he says: There is no god but Allah with no partner, his Lord confirms him and says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me with no partner. When he says: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, his Lord confirms him and says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, to Me belongs dominion and to Me belongs praise. When he says: There is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, He says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, and there is no power nor strength except through Me."
"945","Musab ibn Miqdam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Farra, from al-Agharr, the same as the hadith of Abu Ishaq, except that he added in it, he said: Whoever says them in his illness and then dies will not enter the Fire."
"946","Ali ibn Asim informed me, Abu Harun al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I went out for the dawn prayer and Satan met me in the vestibule of the mosque and crowded against me until I could feel his hair. I seized him and throttled him until I could feel the coldness of his tongue on my hand. Were it not for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have been left dead in the morning for you to look at."
"947","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu Harun al-Abdi narrated to us, Abu Said narrated to us, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and whenever he traveled a farsakh he would shorten the prayer."
"948","Husayn al-Jufi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Iyad: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you strikes his servant and he mentions Allah, Exalted and Mighty, let him lift his hand."
"949","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa, peace be upon them both, disputed with one another. Musa said: You are the vicegerent of Allah; with His Hand He settled you in His Paradise and made His angels prostrate to you, yet you expelled your offspring from Paradise and made them wretched. Adam, peace be upon him, said: You are Musa, whom Allah chose with His speech and His messages; do you blame me for something that was decreed for me before I was created? He said: So Adam overcame Musa in argument, so Adam overcame Musa in argument."
"950","Abu Nuaym and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri informed us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"951","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of the Messenger, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"952","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, who said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr with the two shortest surahs of the Quran. I said: O Messenger of Allah, today you led us in a prayer you never used to pray. He said: I heard the sound of a child crying in the womens rows."
"953","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri informed us, from Sufyan, from Abu Harun, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you strikes his servant and he mentions Allah, Exalted and Mighty, let him lift his hand."
"954","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Abu Harun, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of the prayer — I do not know whether before the taslim or after the taslim: Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they ascribe, and peace be upon the messengers, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"955","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Abu Jafar al-Razi informed us, from Abu Harun, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: There was a weak man among the Muhajirun who had a need from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he wanted to meet him in private to express his need to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was encamped at al-Batha and would come at night and circumambulate the House, until when it was near dawn he would return and lead them in the morning prayer. He said: Circumambulation detained him one night until morning came. When he mounted his camel, the man blocked his way and seized the halter of his she-camel, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need from you. He said: You will attain your need. But he refused, and when he feared he would detain him, he struck him lightly with the whip, then went on and led them in the morning prayer. When he finished, he turned his face toward the people — and when he did that they knew something had happened — so the people gathered around him. He said: Where is the one I struck just now? He repeated it: If he is among the people, let him stand. He said: The man began saying: I seek refuge with Allah and then with His Messenger, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: Come near, come near, until he came near to him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat before him and handed him the whip, saying: Take your retaliation for your lashing and exact retribution. He said: I seek refuge with Allah from striking His Prophet. He said: Take your retaliation for your lashing; there is no harm upon you. He said: I seek refuge with Allah from striking His Prophet. He said: Unless you pardon. He said: Then he threw down the whip and said: I have pardoned, O Messenger of Allah. Then Abu Dharr stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you remember the night of al-Aqabah when I was driving your mount while you were asleep? Whenever I drove her she slowed, and whenever I took her halter she resisted, so I struck you lightly with the whip and said: The people have come to you, and you said: There is no harm upon you. Take, O Messenger of Allah, and exact retribution. He said: I have pardoned. He said: Exact retribution, for it is dearer to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him, and I saw him wincing from the strike of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said: O people, fear Allah, for by Allah, no believer wrongs a believer except that Allah will avenge him on the Day of Resurrection."
"956","Ali ibn Asim informed us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam at the end of his prayer, he would say: Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they ascribe, and peace be upon the messengers, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"957","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: Prayer was enjoined upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night he was taken by night as fifty prayers, then it was reduced until it was made five. Then Allah, Exalted and Mighty, said to him: For you, five counts as fifty; a good deed is rewarded tenfold."
"958","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, who said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of sitting in the streets. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot do without our gatherings in which we converse. He said: If you insist on the gathering, then give the street its due. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the due of the street? He said: Lowering the gaze, withholding harm, returning the greeting, and enjoining good and forbidding evil."
"959","Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam informed us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things do not break the fast of the fasting person: vomiting, cupping, and a wet dream."
"960","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man, from Abu Said, who said: A man placed his hand upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: By Allah, I can hardly bear to place my hand upon you because of the severity of your fever. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, the company of the prophets, have our tribulation doubled just as our reward is doubled. There was a prophet among the prophets who would be afflicted with lice until they killed him, and there was a prophet among the prophets who would be afflicted with poverty until he would take a cloak and wrap himself in it. They used to rejoice in tribulation just as you rejoice in ease."
"961","Musa ibn Masud narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said and Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No fatigue, nor illness, nor anxiety, nor grief, nor harm, nor sorrow befalls the Muslim person, even a thorn that pricks him, except that Allah expiates some of his sins thereby."
"962","Ibrahim ibn al-Ashath narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad informed us, who said: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The earth on the Day of Resurrection will be a single loaf of bread which the Almighty will turn over as one of you turns over his loaf on a journey, as a welcoming portion for the people of Paradise. He said: Then a scholar from the Jews came and said: May the Most Merciful bless you, O Abu al-Qasim, shall I not tell you of the welcoming portion of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Yes, indeed. He said: The earth will be a single loaf of bread, just as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at us and laughed until his molar teeth were visible. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of their condiment? They said: Yes, indeed. He said: Their condiment is balam and nun. They said: What is that? He said: A bull and a whale; seventy thousand will eat from the extra lobe of their livers."
"963","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Musab, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no morning except that two angels call out: Woe to men on account of women, and woe to women on account of men."
"964","Safwan ibn Isa informed us, from Unays, from his father, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us during the illness in which he died with his head bandaged. He said: I followed him until he ascended the minbar, and he said: I am now standing at the Hawd. Then he said: A servant was offered the world and its adornments but chose the Hereafter. He said: None of the people understood except Abu Bakr, who said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; rather we would ransom you with ourselves, our wealth, and our children. He said: Then he descended from the minbar, and he was not seen again until that hour."
"965","Husayn narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Qazah, from Abu Said, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no prayer after two prayers: after Fajr until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"966","Yala narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The truthful, trustworthy merchant will be with the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs."
"967","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Iyad ibn Abd Allah ibn Sad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts the Day of Arafah, Allah will forgive him two years: a year before it and a year after it."
"968","Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum al-Ifriqi narrated to us, who said: Abd Allah ibn Rashid, a freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, narrated to me, who said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted, there is a Tablet containing three hundred and fifteen laws. The Most Merciful says: By My Might and Majesty, no servant of Mine who does not associate anything with Me comes to life upholding even one of them except that I shall admit him to Paradise."
"969","Shuja ibn al-Walid ibn Qays al-Sakuni narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you finishes his prayer in the mosque, let him assign a share of his prayer to his house, for Allah, Exalted and Mighty, will place goodness in his house through his prayer."
"970","Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you finishes his prayer in the mosque, let him assign a share of his prayer to his house, for Allah, Exalted and Mighty, will place goodness in his house through his prayer in his house."
"971","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you belittle himself by seeing a matter concerning Allah, Exalted and Mighty, about which he ought to speak but does not stand up for it; then he will meet Allah, Exalted and Mighty, and He will say: What prevented you from speaking on such-and-such a day? He will say: O Lord, fear of people. He will say: It was Me whom you should rather have feared."
"972","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you belittle himself by seeing a matter of Allah about which there is something to be said and not standing up for it; it will be said to him: What prevented you from speaking about such-and-such? He will say: Fear of people. He will say: It was Me whom you should rather have feared."
"973","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn Umarah, from Abu Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prompt your dying ones to say: There is no god but Allah."
"974","Jafar ibn Awn informed us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, who said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Nahhar ibn Abd Allah al-Abdi, who said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, will question the servant on the Day of Resurrection, and among what He will question him about He will say: What prevented you, when you saw wrongdoing, from denouncing it? When he is prompted with his proof, he will say: O Lord, I feared people but placed my trust in You."
"975","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Said, who said: A man said: Which people are best, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A believer who strives with himself and his wealth in the cause of Allah. He said: Then who? He said: Then a man who withdraws in a mountain valley, worshipping his Lord and sparing people from his harm."
"976","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Maymun, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A mans prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees; if he prays it in a desert land, completing its ablution, bowing, and prostration, his prayer reaches fifty degrees."
"977","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Abi Ayyash, from Abu Said, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who fasts a day in the cause of Allah, seeking the Face of Allah, Exalted and Mighty, except that Allah will distance his face from the Fire by ninety autumns, or seventy autumns."
"978","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Utbah narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more shy than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we would recognize it in his face."
"979","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Sahba, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Said, in a marfu report, who said: When the son of Adam wakes in the morning, all the limbs humble themselves before the tongue, saying: Fear Allah concerning us; if you are upright we shall be upright, and if you are crooked we shall be crooked."
"980","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, who said: Malik narrated to me, from Ayyub ibn Habib, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Juhani, who said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam said to Abu Said al-Khudri: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding blowing into drinks? He said: Yes. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot quench my thirst in a single breath. He said: Then remove the cup from your mouth and breathe. He said: What if there is a speck in it? He said: Then pour it out."
"981","Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qanabi narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah al-Ansari, who said: Abu Said was informed of a funeral among his people, and he seemed to delay until people had taken their seats, then he came. When the people saw him they moved away from around him, and some of them stood so he could sit in their place. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of gatherings are the most spacious. Then he withdrew and sat in a spacious place."
"982","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Numan narrated to us, who said: Abu Said, the freedman of al-Mahri, narrated to me, who said: A brother of mine died leaving dependents but no wealth, so I went to Abu Said al-Khudri and said: A brother of mine has died leaving dependents but no wealth, and I intend to take them out to one of the garrison towns. He said to me: Woe to you, do not take them out, for I heard him saying — meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever endures its hardship and severity with patience, I shall be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"983","Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, who said: Ismail ibn Rafi narrated to me, from Sulayman, the freedman of Abu Said al-Khudri, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, will not accept prayer from a drinker of wine so long as any of it remains in his body."
"984","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Shall I not point you to that by which Allah expiates sins and increases good deeds? They said: Yes, indeed. He said: Performing ablution thoroughly despite hardships, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for one prayer after another. There is none among you who leaves his house in a state of purity and prays with the Muslims a congregational prayer, then remains in his place waiting for another prayer, except that the angels say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. When you stand for prayer, straighten your rows and close the gaps, for I see you from behind my back. When your imam says: Allah is Greatest, say: Allah is Greatest; when he bows, bow; when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise. O company of women, when the men prostrate, lower your gazes and do not look at the private parts of men on account of tight waist-wrappers."
"985","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban informed me that Wasi ibn Habban informed him that Abu Said al-Khudri informed him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbade you from the meat of sacrificial animals, so now eat and store; I forbade you from visiting graves, so now visit them, for in them is a lesson; and I forbade you from nabidh, so now prepare nabidh, but I do not permit you any intoxicant."
"986","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamzah ibn Abi Said, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying upon the minbar: What is the matter with people who say that the kinship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will not benefit on the Day of Resurrection? Yes indeed, by Allah, my kinship is joined in this world and the Hereafter. O people, I shall precede you on the Day of Resurrection at the Hawd. When you come, a man will say: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, and another will say: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. Then I shall say: As for lineage, I recognized it, but you innovated after me and turned back on your heels."
"987","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, who said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to me, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Muhammad narrating from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Honor goats, wipe the dust from them, and pray in their resting place, for they are among the riding beasts of Paradise."
"988","Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to me, who said: Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to me, from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt, who said: Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is married for one of three qualities: a woman is married for her wealth, a woman is married for her beauty, and a woman is married for her religion. So take the one with religion and character; may your right hand be dusted."
"989","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abu al-Khattab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he said: In the year of Tabuk, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people while leaning his back against a palm tree, and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of people and the worst of people? Among the best of people is a man who strives in the cause of Allah on horseback, or on camelback, or on foot, until death comes to him. And among the worst of people is a wicked man who recites the Book of Allah but is not restrained by anything in it."
"990","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer."
"991","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last to come out of the Fire will be two men. Allah, Exalted and Mighty, will say to one of them: O son of Adam, what did you prepare for this Day? Did you do any good or place hope in Me? He will say: No, O Lord. Then he will be ordered to the Fire, and he will be the most regretful of the people of Hellfire. And He will say to the other: O son of Adam, what did you prepare for this Day? Did you do any good or place hope in Me? He will say: Yes, O Lord; I had hoped that when You brought me out of it, You would not return me to it. Then a tree will be raised for him and he will say: O Lord, settle me beneath this tree so I may shade myself in its shade, eat from its fruit, and drink from its water; and he will covenant with Him not to ask Him for anything else. So He will bring him near to it. Then a tree better than the first and more abundant in water will be raised for him, and he will say: O Lord, this one — I shall not ask You for anything else. Settle me beneath it so I may shade myself in its shade, eat from its fruit, and drink from its water. He will say: O son of Adam, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for anything else? He will say: O Lord, this one — I shall not ask You for anything else. So He will settle him beneath it, and he will covenant with Him not to ask Him for anything else. Then a tree at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two and more abundant, will be raised for him, and he will say: O Lord, I shall not ask You for anything else; settle me beneath it in its shade and I shall drink from its water. He will say: O son of Adam, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for anything else? He will say: O Lord, I shall not ask You for anything else. So he will be settled beneath it, and he will covenant with Him not to ask Him for anything else. Then he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise and will be unable to restrain himself, saying: O my Lord, admit me to Paradise. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say: Ask and wish. So he will ask and wish, and Allah will prompt him with things he had no knowledge of. He will ask and wish for the measure of three days of the days of this world, and He will say: O son of Adam, yours is what you asked. Abu Said al-Khudri said: And the like of it with it; and Abu Hurayrah said: And ten times its like with it. Then one of them said to his companion: Narrate what you heard, and I shall narrate what I heard."
"992","Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, from Layth ibn Sad, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Iyad ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Said: A man bought fruits at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and suffered a loss in them, and a debt became binding upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity to your brother. So they gave charity to him, but it did not cover the payment of his debt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Take what you find, and you have nothing but that."
"993","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah, from his father, from Abu Said, who said: He said: O my son, I see that you love sheep and keep them, so tend them well and tend their nasal mucus. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A time will almost come upon people when sheep will be the best wealth of the Muslim, with which he will follow the mountain peaks and the places of rainfall, fleeing with his religion from tribulations."
"994","Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghatfani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of one who meets me intending to take my wealth? He said: Implore him by Allah three times; if he refuses, then fight him. If he kills you, you will enter Paradise, and if you kill him, he will enter the Fire."
"995","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Umamah, from Abu Said, who said: When Banu Qurayzah came down to the judgment of Sad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him, and he was nearby, so he came on a donkey. When he drew near, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand for your chief. He came and sat beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: These people have come down to your judgment. He said: Then I judge that the fighters be killed and the offspring taken captive. He said: You have judged concerning them with the judgment of the King."
"996","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Musa al-Sulami, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn Ghalib, from Abu Said, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traits never combine in a believer: miserliness and bad character."
"997","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Sasah, who said: My father informed me, who said: Abu Said said to me: O my son, when you are in these deserts, raise your voice with the adhan, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No human, nor jinn, nor stone, nor tree hears it except that it will bear witness for him."
"998","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Muayqib, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take with You a covenant which You will fulfill to me on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You never break the promise. I am only a human being, so whichever Muslim I have harmed, or reviled, or — he said — struck, or cursed, make it a prayer for him, make it a purification for him, and a means of nearness by which You bring him close to You on the Day of Resurrection."
"999","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, who said: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to me, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to me, who said: Abu Hani narrated to me, from Abu Ali, who said: I heard Abu Said saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger, Paradise becomes due for him."
"1000","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, Ibrahim Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessed is he who saw me, and he who saw one who saw me, and he who saw one who saw one who saw me."
"1001","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit the sick and follow the funeral procession; they remind you of the Hereafter."
"1002","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Abu al-Mubarak, from Ata, who said: Abu Said al-Khudri said: Love the poor, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in his supplication: O Allah, keep me alive as a poor man, cause me to die as a poor man, and gather me in the company of the poor."
"1003","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Abu al-Mubarak, from Ata, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has not believed in the Quran who regards its prohibitions as lawful."
"1004","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Ata, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice, then the people sat. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I sacrificed. He said: No harm. Then another came to him and said: I shaved before I stoned. He said: No harm. He said: He was not asked about anything except that he said: No harm. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of Arafah is a place of standing, all of Muzdalifah is a place of standing, all of Mina is a place of sacrifice, and all the mountain passes of Makkah are a path and a place of sacrifice."
"1005","Zakariyya ibn Adi informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Jabir, that a man freed a slave to take effect after his death, then his master became needy, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to sell him. He sold him for eight hundred dirhams, and he said: Spend it upon your dependents, for charity is only from surplus wealth, and begin with those you support."
"1006","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and brought him to the palm trees, where his son Ibrahim was in his mothers lap, breathing his last. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him and placed him in his lap, then said: O Ibrahim, we cannot avail you anything against Allah. Then his eyes shed tears. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you weep? Did you not forbid weeping? He said: No, but I forbade wailing, and two foolish, wicked voices: a voice at the tune of amusement and play and the flutes of Satan, and a voice at a calamity: scratching faces, tearing garments, and the cry of Satan. This is mercy, and whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy. O Ibrahim, were it not that it is a true matter, a truthful promise, a path that must be taken, and that our latter ones will join our former ones, we would have grieved for you with a grief severer than this. We are indeed grieved by you: the eye weeps and the heart grieves, but we do not say what angers the Lord, Exalted and Mighty."
"1007","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he sent me on an errand. I came and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. After a while he returned it to me, saying: Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was praying. He said: And his face was turned away from the qiblah."
"1008","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Munim ibn Nuaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan and Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Bilal: O Bilal, when you call the adhan, proclaim it slowly, and when you call the iqamah, hasten it. Place between your adhan and your iqamah enough time for one eating to finish his food, one drinking to finish his drink, and one relieving himself to finish attending to his need. And do not stand until you see me."
"1009","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Habib al-Muallim, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah grants you the conquest of Makkah, I would pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray here. The man repeated it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once or twice, and when he persisted, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do as you wish."
"1010","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the ear of grain which the wind moves, falling down at times and standing upright at times; and the likeness of the disbeliever is like the cedar tree, remaining upright until it is uprooted."
"1011","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who plants a plant except that it counts as charity for him, whatever is eaten from it, whatever is stolen from it, whatever birds eat from it, and whatever beasts eat from it."
"1012","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The sun eclipsed at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died. The people said: The sun has eclipsed only because of the death of Ibrahim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and led the people in prayer: six bowings with four prostrations. He began, said Allahu Akbar, then recited and prolonged the recitation, then bowed for about as long as he had stood, then raised his head from bowing and recited a recitation shorter than the first recitation, then bowed for about as long as he had stood, then raised his head from bowing and recited a recitation shorter than the second, then bowed for about as long as he had stood, then raised his head from bowing, then went down into prostration and prostrated twice. Then he stood and bowed also three bowings, none of them except that the one before it was longer than the one after it, and his bowing was about equal to his prostration. Then he stepped back, and the rows behind him stepped back until he reached the women. Then he stepped forward, and the people stepped forward with him until he stood in his place. He finished when he finished and the sun had brightened. He said: O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah, and they do not eclipse for the death of any human. When you see anything of that, pray until it clears. There is nothing you are promised except that I have seen it in this prayer of mine. The Fire was brought, and that was when you saw me step back, fearing that its blast might strike me. I even saw in it the man with the hooked staff dragging his intestines in the Fire; he used to steal the belongings of the pilgrims with his hooked staff — if he was noticed, he would say: It only caught on my staff, and if he was unnoticed, he would take it away. I even saw in it the woman with the cat which she tied up: she neither fed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth until it died of hunger. Then Paradise was brought, and that was when you saw me step forward until I stood in my place. I extended my hand, intending to take some of its fruit for you to look at, then it occurred to me not to do so. There is nothing you are promised except that I have seen it in this prayer of mine."
"1013","Musab ibn Miqdam al-Khathami and Abu Nuaym informed us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every servant will be resurrected upon that which he died upon."
"1014","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the five prayers is like a flowing, sweet river at the door of one of you, from which he bathes every day five times."
"1015","Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying three days before his death: Let none of you die except while holding a good opinion of Allah, Exalted and Mighty."
"1016","Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which prayer is best? He said: Lengthy standing in devotion."
"1017","Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fears that he will not wake up at the end of the night, let him perform Witr at the beginning of the night and then sleep; and whoever hopes to wake up at the end of the night, let him perform Witr at the end of the night, for the recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."
"1018","Yala and Muhammad, sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, saying: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: Ubayy ibn Kab fell ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a physician to him, who cauterized him over his medial arm vein."
"1019","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I live, Allah willing, I shall command — or forbid — my nation not to name anyone Nafi, Aflah, or Barakah. Al-Amash said: I do not know whether he mentioned Nafi or not, because when a man comes and says: Is there Barakah here? They say: No."
"1020","Jafar ibn Awn informed us, al-Amash informed us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will surely come upon people when an army goes out and seeks a man from among my Companions. It will be said: Is there among you a man from the Companions of Muhammad? They will say: Yes, so they will seek victory through him and victory will be granted to them. Then a time will come upon people when an army goes out and it will be said: Is there among you a man from the Companions of Muhammad? They will seek him but not find him. Then it will be said: Is there among you anyone who saw anyone from the Companions of Muhammad? They will seek him but not find him. If a man from among my Companions were beyond the sea, they would surely go to him."
"1021","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: Abu Humayd al-Ansari came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a cup containing milk, carrying it uncovered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not cover it, even with a stick laid across it?"
"1022","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Between faith and disbelief lies abandoning prayer."
"1023","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir: Fever came seeking permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Who are you? She said: I am Umm Mildam. He said: Do you know the people of Quba? She said: Yes. He said: Then go to them. He said: So they complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If you wish, I shall supplicate to Allah, Exalted is He, to remove it from you, and if you wish, it will be a purification for you. They said: Rather let it be a purification for us."
"1024","Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to pray two rakahs, making them brief. I said to Sulayman: On Friday? He said: Yes."
"1025","Muhadir ibn al-Muwarra narrated to me, who said: al-Amash narrated to me, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: A boy was born to a man of the Ansar and he named him Muhammad. They said: We shall not call you by the name of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we consult him. They went to him and found that he had fallen from a horse onto wood and his foot had been crushed. They found him in an upper room belonging to Aishah. He said: You have come asking me about such-and-such. They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah. He said: And you mentioned the Hour. They said: That had come up on the way. He said: There is no living soul that a hundred years will pass over."
"1026","Muhadir narrated to me, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I used to perform ruqyah for scorpion stings, but you forbade it. He said: Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother, let him benefit him."
"1027","Muhadir narrated to me, al-A'mash narrated, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while we were on a journey: Indeed in Madinah there are men, you do not cross a valley nor travel a road except that they are with you; sickness has kept them back from you."
"1028","Ibrahim ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to me, al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Sulayman, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a foul-smelling wind blew, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of the hypocrites backbit some of the Muslims, and for that reason this wind was sent; and perhaps he said: for that reason this wind has blown."
"1029","Ibrahim ibn al-Ash'ath narrated, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated, from Sulayman, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a wind blew that almost buried the rider, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This wind has been sent for the death of a hypocrite. When we returned to Madinah we found that a greatly hypocritical hypocrite had died on that day, and I afterwards heard our companions saying it was Rafi' ibn al-Tabut."
"1030","Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people of Paradise eat and drink, and they do not urinate, nor defecate, nor blow their noses, nor spit; their food is followed by belching and perspiration like the sweat of musk; in it they are inspired to glorify Allah and declare His greatness just as they are inspired to breathe."
"1031","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream as if my head had been cut off. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: When one of you is toyed with in his sleep, let him not relate it to people."
"1032","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the caller to prayer calls the adhan, Satan flees until he is at al-Rawha, which is thirty miles from Madinah."
"1033","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Iblis places his throne upon the water, then he sends out his detachments; the nearest of them to him in rank is the greatest of them in trial. He said: One of them comes to him and says: I did such and such, and he says: You have done nothing. He said: Then one of them comes to him and says: I did not leave him until I separated him from his wife, and he says: You are excellent, and he draws him near to himself."
"1034","Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated, from Za'idah, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: When do you pray witr? He said: After the night prayer before I sleep. And he said to Umar: When do you pray witr? He said: At the end of the night. He said: This one has taken precaution and this one has shown strength. Al-Husayn said: He took to precaution."
"1035","Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Jabir who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would return to our homes, which were a mile away, while we could still see the places where the arrows landed."
"1036","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to me, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Zuhr or Asr prayer in our rows, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to take something while he was in prayer, then he stepped back, so the people stepped back. When he finished he was asked by Ubayy ibn Ka'b: O Messenger of Allah, you did something in the prayer that you were not accustomed to do. He said: Paradise was displayed to me with what is in it of splendor, and I reached for a bunch of grapes from it to bring to you, but I was prevented from it; had I brought it to you, those between heaven and earth would have eaten from it without diminishing it. Then the Fire was displayed to me, and when I felt its heat I stepped back from it. Most of those I saw in it were women who, if entrusted, disclose, if they ask, they ask importunately, and if asked, they withhold. And I saw in it Luhayy ibn Amr dragging his intestines in the Fire; and the one I saw who most resembled him was Ma'bad ibn Aktham al-Ka'bi. Ma'bad said: O Messenger of Allah, is it feared for me because of my resemblance to him, and he is my father? He said: No, you are a believer and he is a disbeliever. Luhayy was the first to lead the Arabs to the worship of idols."
"1037","Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: So-and-so has a date-palm stalk in my garden, and it has harmed me and its place has become a hardship for me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him and said: Sell me your date-palm stalk which is in so-and-so's garden. He said: No. He said: Then give it to me as a gift. He said: No. He said: Then sell it to me for a date-palm stalk in Paradise. He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not seen a human being more miserly than you except the one who is miserly with greeting."
"1038","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Husayn ibn Ali narrated, from Za'idah, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, who is Ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call out, O Umar, among the people that whoever dies worshipping Allah sincerely from his heart, He will admit him into Paradise, or He will forbid the Fire for him. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, then they will rely upon it."
"1039","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, do you know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brought your father back to life and said to him: Wish from Me whatever you wish? He said: Let me be returned to the world so that I may be killed once more. He said: I have decreed that they shall not return."
"1040","Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated, from Za'idah, from Layth who said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep until he recited Alif Lam Mim, the revelation of al-Sajdah, and Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the dominion."
"1041","Abu Asim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should die except while having a good opinion of Allah."
"1042","Abu Asim informed, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon A'ishah while she was weeping, and said: What is the matter with you that you weep? She said: I weep because the people have exited ihram and I have not, and they have circumambulated the House and I have not, and this Hajj has come as you see. He said: This is a matter which Allah has decreed upon the daughters of Adam, so bathe and enter ihram for Hajj and perform what the pilgrim performs except that you do not circumambulate the House, nor pray. So she did that, and when she became pure he said: Circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he said: You have exited from your Hajj and your Umrah. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I feel in myself about my Umrah that I did not circumambulate when I performed Hajj. He said: Take her, O Abd al-Rahman, and perform Umrah with her from al-Tan'im."
"1043","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Umar ibn Zayd informed, who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing between the servant and disbelief, or he said: polytheism, except that he abandons a prescribed prayer."
"1044","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Umar ibn Zayd al-San'ani narrated, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating cats and eating their price."
"1045","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The prophets were displayed to me: Moses was a lean, slender man as if he were one of the men of Azd Shanu'ah; and I saw Jesus son of Mary, and the one I saw who most resembled him was Urwah ibn Mas'ud; and I saw Abraham, and the one I saw who most resembled him was your companion, meaning himself; and I saw Gabriel, and the one I saw who most resembled him was Dihyah."
"1046","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, who said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for it does not befit Satan to take my form. And he said: When one of you dreams a dream, let him not inform people of Satan toying with him in the dream."
"1047","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times, seek refuge in Allah from Satan three times, and turn from the side he was upon."
"1048","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came on Friday while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the pulpit, and Sulayk sat before praying, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you bowed two rak'ahs? He said: No. He said: Stand and bow them."
"1049","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best for which riding camels are mounted are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."
"1050","Abu Nu'aym narrated, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated, from Jabir, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever has an imam, the recitation of the imam is recitation for him."
"1051","Abu Nu'aym narrated, al-Umari narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer in a single garment wrapped around himself."
"1052","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Himmani narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A person is in prayer as long as he waits for it."
"1053","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed, from Isma'il ibn Abd al-Malik, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not relieve himself until he had gone out of sight and could not be seen. We stopped in a desert land with no tree nor landmark, so he said: O Jabir, put water in your waterskin then come with us. He said: So we went until we could not be seen, when there were two trees with four cubits between them. He said: O Jabir, go to this tree and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says to you: Join your companion so that I may sit behind you both. So it returned to it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat behind them; then they returned to their places. Then we rode with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among us as if birds shaded us. A woman met him with a boy, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son here is seized by Satan three times every day. He stopped for her, then took the boy and placed him between himself and the front of the saddle, then said: Get out, enemy of Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah, three times, then he handed him back to her. When we finished our journey we passed by that place, and the woman met us with her boy and with two rams she was driving, and said: O Messenger of Allah, accept my gift from me, for by Him Who sent you with the truth, it has not returned to him since. He said: Take one of them from her and return the other to her. He said: Then we traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among us as if birds shaded us, when a stray camel appeared until, when it was between the two rows, it fell prostrate. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat, then turned to the people and said: Who is the owner of the camel? Some youths of the Ansar came forward and said: It is ours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What is its condition? They said: We have used it for drawing water for twenty years, and it had a little fat, so we wanted to slaughter it and distribute it among our boys, but it escaped from us. He said: Will you sell it to me? They said: No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: As for me, treat it well until its term comes to it. The Muslims said at that: O Messenger of Allah, then we are more entitled to prostrate than the beasts. He said: It is not fitting to prostrate to anything; had that been so, I would have commanded women to prostrate to their husbands."
"1054","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A person is with the one he loves."
"1055","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The augury of every servant is upon his neck."
"1056","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear these sandals often, for one of you remains as if mounted as long as he wears sandals."
"1057","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah informed, from Abu al-Zubayr who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, after we had returned from the expedition of Tabuk: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Madinah there are peoples, you do not travel a distance nor cross a valley except that they were with you; sickness kept them back."
"1058","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: Some people whose homes were far from the mosque complained of that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Remain in your place, for indeed for you is a good deed for every step."
"1059","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade food to be sold until two measures have passed over it: the measure of the seller and the measure of the buyer."
"1060","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two that necessitate? He said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, Paradise is necessitated for him; and whoever dies associating something with Allah, the Fire is necessitated for him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is most excellent? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. He said: Which prayer is most excellent? He said: Lengthy standing. He said: Which jihad is most excellent? He said: The one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed. He said: Which emigration is most excellent? He said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes."
"1061","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated, Abu al-Zubayr narrated, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a woman, then entered upon Zaynab bint Jahsh and fulfilled his need with her, then went out to his Companions and said to them: A woman comes in the form of Satan and turns away in the form of Satan, so whoever feels that, let him go to his wife, for indeed that dispels what is in his soul."
"1062","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated, Abu al-Zubayr narrated, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, not associating anything with Him, Allah will admit him into Paradise; and whoever meets Him associating something with Him, He will admit him into the Fire."
"1063","Muhammad ibn Munib al-Adani narrated to me, al-Sari ibn Yahya informed, from Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the chief supplication for forgiveness: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You; You created me and I am Your servant; I am upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able; I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done; I acknowledge to You Your blessing upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me; indeed none forgives sins but You."
"1064","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated, from Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: I fell ill while I had seven sisters with me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and blew upon my face, so I recovered. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not bequeath two-thirds for my sisters? He said: Withhold. I said: Half? He said: Withhold. Then he went out and left me, and said: O Jabir, I do not think you will die from this illness of yours; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has sent down and clarified for your sisters, and made for them two-thirds. Jabir used to say: This verse was revealed concerning me: They ask you for a ruling; say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning kalalah."
"1065","Sa'id ibn Sallam narrated to me, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated, Abu al-Zubayr narrated, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took part in twenty-one expeditions."
"1066","Umar ibn Sa'd narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is invited to food, let him accept; if he wishes he may eat, and if he wishes he may leave it."
"1067","Umar ibn Sa'd narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove the harm from it and not leave it for Satan, and let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or gives it to be licked, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies."
"1068","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating leeks, onions, and garlic. He said: The angels are harmed by what the children of Adam are harmed by."
"1069","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, Ayyub narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me when a camel of mine had become exhausted for me. He said: He supplicated with whatever he wished, then said: Ride. Then he prodded it with a stick he had. He said: So it leapt up, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold on. He said: I began to restrain it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so that I might hear his speech. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: Will you sell me your camel, O Jabir? I said: Yes, I will sell it to you for five ounces, with its use for me until I arrive. He said: So he granted me its use until I arrived; when I came to him he paid me five ounces in cash and added a qirat for me, then he gifted it back to me afterwards."
"1070","Salih ibn Abdullah narrated to me, al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa'."
"1071","Salih ibn Abdullah narrated, al-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and A'ishah used to bathe from a single vessel."
"1072","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every Muslim in every seven days is a bath on one day, and that is Friday."
"1073","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hushaym narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man should spend the night with a woman except that he is her husband or her mahram."
"1074","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, from Hajjaj, from Abu al-Zubayr and Ata, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling what is on the tops of palm trees for measured dates."
"1075","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plastering the grave, sitting upon it, and building over it; and Sulayman ibn Musa said: and writing upon it."
"1076","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abraham, peace be upon him, made the House of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sacred and secure, and I have made Madinah sacred, between its two lava tracts; its thorny trees are not to be cut, nor its game to be hunted."
"1077","Umar ibn Sa'd narrated, from Sufyan, from Aban, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, then with it, and blessed; and whoever bathes, then that is more excellent."
"1078","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night while his Companions were waiting for him for the last night prayer, and said: The people have slept and lain down while you wait for the prayer; indeed you are in prayer as long as you wait for it; were it not for the weakness of the weak and the age of the aged, I would have delayed this prayer until midnight."
"1079","Yazid ibn Harun informed, Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj informed, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, there was a crowd and a man who had been shaded over, so he asked about him, and they said: He is fasting. He said: Righteousness is not to fast while traveling."
"1080","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only established preemption in everything undivided; when the boundaries fall and the roads are arranged, there is no preemption."
"1081","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray over a man with a debt upon him. He said: A deceased was brought, so he asked: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So he prayed over him. When Allah granted victory to His Messenger, he said: I am closer to every believer than his own self; whoever leaves a debt, it is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."
"1082","Abd al-Razzaq informed, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a resting place, and the people dispersed among the thorny trees seeking shade beneath them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hung his weapon upon a tree, when a Bedouin came to his sword and took it and drew it, then turned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Who will protect you from me? He said: Allah. The Bedouin said two or three times: Who will protect you from me, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah. He said: The Bedouin sheathed the sword, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called his Companions and informed them of the Bedouin's deed while he sat beside him; he did not punish him."
"1083","Yazid ibn Harun informed, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali informed, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good deed is charity; what a Muslim spends of his expenditure upon himself and his family is written for him as charity; what a Muslim man protects his honor with is written for him as charity; and every expenditure a Muslim spends, its replacement is guaranteed by Allah, except expenditure upon building or disobedience. He said: I said to Ibn al-Munkadir: What is his saying: What a Muslim man protects his honor with? He said: That he gives to a poet and a foul-tongued person. He said: I only know that he said: The God-fearing. [FLAG: final epithet truncated/garbled in source]"
"1084","Yazid ibn Harun informed, Shu'bah informed, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a debt upon my father, so I knocked on the door. He said: Who is this? I said: I. He said: I, as if he disliked it."
"1085","Ja'far ibn Awn informed, Isma'il ibn Muslim informed, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid at sleep, for it strengthens the sight and grows the hair."
"1086","Uthman ibn Umar informed, Abdullah ibn Amir informed, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? The best of you are the longest of you in age and the best of you in deeds."
"1087","Abu Nu'aym informed, and Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked for anything at all and said: No."
"1088","Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will bring me news of the people on the day of al-Ahzab? Al-Zubayr said: I. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will bring me news of the people? Al-Zubayr said: I. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will bring me news of the people? Al-Zubayr said: I. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a disciple, and indeed my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"1089","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to me, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrating from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us istikhara just as he taught us a surah of the Qur'an, saying: When one of you intends a matter, let him bow two rak'ahs apart from the obligatory, then let him say: O Allah, I seek good from You through Your knowledge, I seek ability through Your power, and I ask You of Your immense bounty; for You decree and I do not decree, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if You know this matter - naming whatever thing he intends - to be good for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affair, or he said: good for me in my immediate affair and my later one, then decree it for me, make it easy for me, and bless me in it; and if You know - saying the like of what he said the first time - and if it is evil, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, decree good for me wherever it is, then make me pleased with it."
"1090","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, al-Munkadir narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good deed is charity; among good deeds are that you meet your brother with a cheerful face, and that you pour from your bucket into your brother's vessel."
"1091","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated, from Talhah ibn Amr who said: Ibn al-Munkadir informed me, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most excellent faith before Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is faith in Allah, jihad in His path, and an accepted Hajj. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the righteousness of Hajj? He said: Feeding food and gentle speech."
"1092","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of a leper and placed it with him in the bowl, and said: Eat, in the name of Allah, trusting in Allah and relying upon Him."
"1093","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ask Allah for beneficial knowledge, and seek refuge in Allah from knowledge that does not benefit."
"1094","Yazid ibn Harun narrated, Yazid ibn Iyad narrated, from Zayd ibn Hasan, that he narrated to them that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment wrapped around himself as a waist-wrapper."
"1095","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, Qatadah narrated, from Sulayman al-Yashkuri, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses a wall around land, it belongs to him."
"1096","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Muharib Khassafah at Nakhl, and they saw a moment of heedlessness from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a man of them called Ghawrath ibn al-Harith came until he stood over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a sword and said: Who will protect you from me? He said: Allah. The sword fell from him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the sword and said to him: Who will protect you from me? He said: Be the best of takers. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? He said: No, but I pledge to you that I shall not fight you, nor be with a people who fight you. He said: So he released him, and he came to his companions and said: I have come to you from the best of people. When it was noon or afternoon - Abu Awanah doubted - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the prayer of fear. He said: The people were two groups: a group facing their enemy, and a group praying with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He prayed with the group with him two rak'ahs, then they left and took the place of those, and those came and prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rak'ahs. So for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it was four rak'ahs and for the people two rak'ahs."
"1097","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah seventy camels, each camel on behalf of seven."
"1098","Yazid ibn Harun informed, Shu'bah informed, from Muharib ibn Dithar that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and we were with him; when we arrived at Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, enter the mosque and pray two rak'ahs. He said: So I came to the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs."
"1099","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated, Mis'ar narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) owed me a debt, so he paid me and increased me. Mis'ar said: I think he said: I came to him in the forenoon while he was in the mosque. He said: Go and pray, or: pray two rak'ahs."
"1100","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, Muharib ibn Dithar narrated, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a camel from a man and gave him extra."
"1101","Umar ibn Sa'd narrated, from Sufyan, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to come to his family by night or to seek out their faults."
"1102","Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar who said: I heard Jabir saying: Mu'adh prayed Maghrib with his people and began with al-Baqarah or al-Nisa; a man came when night had fallen, with a water-carrying camel of his, so he left the camel and joined them in prayer. When he saw that he had lengthened, fearing for his camel he prayed alone then left before him. It reached that man that Mu'adh said of him: Hypocrite. So that man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you a causer of trial? Are you a causer of trial? Or he said: Are you a tempter? Why did you not pray, or: recite, Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, By the sun and its brightness, and By the night when it covers - Shu'bah doubted concerning al-Shams or al-Layl, one of them - behind you pray the aged, the needy, and the weak."
"1103","Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity in less than five ounces, no charity in less than five camels, and no charity in less than five wasqs."
"1104","Abu Nu'aym narrated to me, Ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Amr: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: We were on the day of al-Hudaybiyah one thousand four hundred. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are today the best people of the earth."
"1105","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Kalbi, from Abu Salih, from Jabir ibn Abdullah ibn Ri'ab: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning this verse: For them is glad tidings in the life of the world. He said: It is the righteous dream which the servant sees or which is seen for him."
"1106","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Ghalib ibn Sulayman narrated, from Kathir ibn Ziyad al-Bursani, from Abu Sumayyah who said: We differed here in Basra concerning the passing over Hell. A group said: No believer enters it, and others said: They all pass over it. So I met Jabir ibn Abdullah and asked him about that. He said: They all pass over it, then Allah saves those who feared Him and leaves the wrongdoers therein kneeling. I said: We differed concerning it in Basra; a people said: No believer enters it, and others said: They all enter it. He pointed with his two fingers to his ears and said: May they be deafened if I did not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The passing is the entering; none righteous nor wicked remains except that he enters it; it becomes coolness and peace upon the believers just as it was upon Abraham, until Hell - or the Fire - has a clamor from their coldness; then Allah saves those who feared Him and leaves the wrongdoers therein kneeling."
"1107","Habban ibn Hilal narrated to me, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated, Umar ibn Abdullah, freedman of Ghufrah, narrated, from Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Safwan al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has detachments of angels who alight and stand over the gatherings of remembrance in the earth, so graze in the meadows of Paradise. They said: And where are the meadows of Paradise? He said: The gatherings of remembrance; go and return in the remembrance of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and remember Him by yourselves. Whoever wishes to know his station with Allah, let him look at how the station of Allah is with him; for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, places the servant with Himself where he has placed Him with himself."
"1108","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to me, who said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, Haram ibn Uthman narrated, from the two sons of Jabir, from their father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the door of his room, let him give greeting, for his companion of the devils with him returns; when you enter your rooms, give greeting, so that its devilish inhabitant leaves; when you depart, name Allah over the first cloth you place upon your mounts so that Satan does not share your mount with you, for if you do not do so he shares it with you; when you eat, name Allah so that he does not share your food with you, for if you do not do so he shares your food with you; do not leave garbage overnight with you in your rooms, for it is his seat; do not leave the hand-towel overnight with you in your houses, for it is his bed; do not spread the cloths that touch the backs of mounts; do not dwell in houses without locks; do not sleep upon roofs without walls; and when you hear the barking of a dog or the braying of an ass, seek refuge in Allah, for no ass brays nor dog barks until they see him."
"1109","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated, al-A'mash narrated, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was driving a camel of mine at the rear of the people, limping or ailing. He said: What is its condition? I said: O Messenger of Allah, it limps or has ailed. He took something in his hand and struck it, then said: Ride. I kept holding it back until they caught up with me. When between us and Madinah there was a stop and we camped in the evening, I wanted to hasten to my family. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where to? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am newly married, so I wanted to hasten to my family. He said to me: Do not come to your family by night. Then he asked me: Did you marry a virgin or a previously married woman? He said: I said: Rather a previously married woman. He said: Why not a virgin whom you play with and who plays with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah died and left young girls with me, so I disliked marrying one like them to them, and I wanted an intelligent woman who had experience. He did not say: You did well, nor: You did badly. Then he said: Sell me your camel. I said: No, rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Sell it to me. I said: No, rather it is yours. When he pressed me, I said: So-and-so has an ounce of gold with me, so it is yours for it. Then he said: Use it to reach your family. He said: When I arrived at Madinah I brought it to him, and he commanded Bilal to give me an ounce, and to increase me, so Bilal added a qirat for me. I said: This is something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) added for me; it shall never leave me, so I placed it in the purse. On the day of al-Harrah the people of Syria took it among what they took."
"1110","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the Friday prayer when a caravan entered Madinah, so they turned and went out to it until none remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of them except twelve men. Then this verse was revealed: And when they see trade or amusement, they disperse to it and leave you standing."
"1111","Amr ibn Awn narrated to me, from Hushaym, from Husayn, from Abu Sufyan and Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: And they leave you standing. He said: A caravan came, so they dispersed to it, and none remained except twelve men."
"1112","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: A boy was born to a man of the Ansar, so he named him al-Qasim. The Ansar said: By Allah, we shall never call you by it. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he praised the Ansar with good, then said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"1113","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Mansur, from Salim, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of you comes to me and asks me, so I give him, and he departs carrying in his embrace nothing but the Fire."
"1114","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A mudd suffices for ablution, and a sa' for major impurity. A man said: It does not suffice us. He said: It sufficed one better than you and with more hair."
"1115","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated, from Amr ibn Murrah and Husayn; they heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd saying: I heard Jabir saying: Thirst struck us and we wept aloud, then we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He placed his hand in water, and the water began to gush as if springs from between his fingers, and said: Mention the name of Allah. So we drank until we were satisfied and it sufficed us. Shu'bah said: In the hadith of Amr ibn Murrah: We said to Jabir: How many were you? He said: We were one thousand five hundred; had we been a hundred thousand, it would have sufficed us."
"1116","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the entire year."
"1117","With its chain, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor of the Muslims enter Paradise before the rich by forty autumns."
"1118","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who flees from the plague is like the one who flees from battle, and the patient therein is like the patient in battle."
"1119","Zayd ibn Hubab al-Ukli informed, who said: Layth ibn Sa'd informed me, who said: al-Zuhri informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: On the day of Uhud, one man and two men would be shrouded in a single garment; they were shrouded with their wounds, buried, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray over them."
"1120","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with something like an egg of gold and said: This is charity, and I have no wealth besides it. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw it at him with it, and said: One of you goes and strips himself of his wealth, then becomes a dependent upon people."
"1121","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated, from Asim ibn Umar, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came with something like an egg of gold which he had found in one of the raids, and brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his right side, and said: O Messenger of Allah, take it from me as charity, for by Allah I have nothing besides it. He turned away from him; then he came to him from his left side and said the like of that; then he came to him from before him and said the like of that. He said: Bring it, in anger, and threw it at him with a throw that, had it struck him, would have wounded or hurt him. Then he said: One of you comes with his wealth, owning nothing besides it, and gives it in charity, then sits afterwards begging from people. Charity is only from sufficiency. Take what is yours; we have no need of it. So the man took his wealth and went."
"1122","Ya'la narrated, al-Ajlah narrated, from al-Dhayyal ibn Harmalah, from Jabir who said: We came with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a journey until we reached a garden of the gardens of Banu al-Najjar, when there was a camel therein against which none entered the garden except that it charged at him. They mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came to it and called it; it came placing its lip upon the ground until it knelt before him. He said: Bring a halter. He haltered it and handed it to its owner, then turned and said: There is nothing between heaven and earth except that it knows that I am the Messenger of Allah, except the disobedient of jinn and men."
"1123","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Ajlah, from al-Dhayyal ibn Harmalah al-Asadi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: Quraysh gathered one day and said: Look for the most knowledgeable of you in magic, soothsaying, and poetry, let him go to this man who has divided our unity, scattered our affair, and faulted our religion; let him speak to him and see what he replies. They said: We know none but Utbah ibn Rabi'ah. They said: You, O Abu al-Walid. Utbah came to him and said: O Muhammad, are you better, or Abdullah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. Then he said: Are you better, or Abd al-Muttalib? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. He said: If you claim that they are better than you, they worshipped the gods you have faulted; and if you claim that you are better than them, then speak so that we may hear your saying. By Allah, we have never seen an infant more ill-omened to his people than you: you have divided our unity, scattered our affair, faulted our religion, and exposed us among the Arabs until it has spread among them that among Quraysh is a magician, and that among Quraysh is a soothsayer. By Allah, we await nothing but like the cry of a woman in labor, that some of us rise against others with swords until we annihilate one another. O man, if it is need that is with you, we shall gather for you until you are the richest single man of Quraysh; and if it is desire for women that is with you, choose whichever women of Quraysh you wish and we shall marry you to ten. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you finished? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate: Ha Mim, a revelation from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, until he reached: But if they turn away, then say: I have warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud. Utbah said: Enough, enough; is there nothing with you besides this? He said: No. So he returned to Quraysh, and they said: What is behind you? He said: I have left nothing which I thought you would address him with except that I have addressed him. They said: Did he answer you? He said: Yes. He said: No, by Him Who set it up as a building, I understood nothing of what he said except that he said: I have warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud. They said: Woe to you, the man speaks to you in Arabic and you do not know what he said? He said: No, by Allah, I understood nothing of what he said except the mention of the thunderbolt."
"1124","Ya'la and Muhammad, sons of Ubayd, narrated, both said: Mis'ar narrated, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon his mount wherever its face was."
"1125","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated, Mis'ar narrated, from Yazid al-Faqir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: Weeping women came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Allah, give us rain, relieving, wholesome, fruitful, immediate and not delayed, beneficial and not harmful. Then it poured upon them."
"1126","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from a man, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep yourselves and your families in houses at the early onset of the night, for the jinn spread therein."
"1127","Ya'la ibn Ubayd informed, Abu Bakr al-Madani informed, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to use the toothstick at night two or three times; whenever he slept and awoke, he used the toothstick, performed ablution, and bowed two rak'ahs or rak'ahs."
"1128","Ya'la informed, Abu Bakr narrated, from Jabir who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we looked at the twilight."
"1129","Ya'la informed, Abu Bakr informed, from Jabir who said: A man from al-Awali came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Gabriel were praying where the funeral prayer is performed. When he finished, the man said: O Messenger of Allah, who is this whom I saw with you? He said: Have you seen him? He said: Yes. He said: You have seen much good; this is Gabriel. He has continued to enjoin upon me the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"1130","Ya'la narrated, Abu Bakr narrated, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine the first prayer and Asr while traveling."
"1131","Ya'la informed, Abu Bakr narrated, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is sacred like the sacredness of Makkah; by Him Who sent down upon Muhammad, upon its mountain passes are angels guarding it from Satan."
"1132","Ja'far ibn Awn informed, Musa ibn Ubaydah informed, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from his father who said: Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make me like the cup of the rider; when the rider hangs his belongings, he takes his cup and fills it with water: if he has need of ablution he performs ablution, if he has need of drinking he drinks, otherwise he pours out what is in it. Place me in the beginning of supplication, in the middle of supplication, and in the end of supplication."
"1133","Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed, Ibn Jurayj informed, who said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad informed me that he heard his father narrating that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drove sacrificial animals in his Hajj, slaughtered sixty-three with his hand, commanded Ali ibn Abi Talib, who slaughtered the rest; Ali had driven sacrificial animals for him, the total of all that being one hundred camels."
"1134","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, who said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad informed me, hearing his father narrating that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah narrating: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted one hundred camels in his Hajj, commanded a piece from each camel, so they were placed in the pot, and they ate of its meat and drank of its broth. I said: Who is the one who ate with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and drank of the broth? He said: Ali; Ja'far says it."
"1135","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hatim ibn Isma'il al-Madani narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father who said: We entered upon Jabir ibn Abdullah, and he asked about the people until he reached me. I said: I am Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn. He stretched his hand to my head, undid my upper button, then undid my lower button, then placed his palms between my breasts while I was then a young lad. He said: Welcome to you, O son of my brother; ask whatever you wish. So I asked him while he was blind, and the time of prayer came. He stood in a woven sheet wrapped in it; whenever he placed it upon his shoulders its ends returned to him because of its smallness, while his cloak was beside him upon the clothes-rack. He led us in prayer. I said: Inform me about the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He motioned with his hand and counted nine, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained nine years without performing Hajj, then it was announced among the people in the tenth year that the Messenger of Allah would perform Hajj. A large number of people came to Madinah, all seeking to follow the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and to act like his acting. We went out with him until we reached Dhu al-Hulayfah, where Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr. She sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What shall I do? He said: Bathe, wrap yourself with a cloth, and enter ihram. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the mosque, then mounted al-Qaswa until, when his camel stood straight with him upon al-Bayda, I looked as far as my sight reached before him of riders and walkers, likewise to his right, likewise to his left, and likewise behind him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, the Qur'an descended upon him, he knew its interpretation, and whatever he acted of it we acted. He entered ihram with tawhid: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You, here I am; indeed praise and bounty are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You. The people entered ihram with this with which they enter ihram, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reject anything of it from them; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept to his talbiyah. Jabir said: We intended nothing but Hajj; we did not know Umrah, until we reached the House with him. He touched the Corner, walked briskly three times and walked four, then advanced to the Station of Abraham and recited: And take the Station of Abraham as a place of prayer. He placed the Station between himself and the House - my father used to say, and I do not know whether he mentioned it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he recited in the two rak'ahs: Say: He is Allah, One, and Say: O disbelievers. Then he returned to the Corner and touched it, then went out through the gate to al-Safa. When he drew near al-Safa he recited: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah. I begin with what Allah began with. He began with al-Safa, ascended it until he saw the House, faced the qiblah, declared the unity of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and magnified Him, and said: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner has He; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things; there is no god but Allah alone, He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone. Then he supplicated between that, saying the like of this three times. Then he descended to al-Marwah until his feet poured forth to the bottom of the valley; when we ascended we walked until he reached al-Marwah, and did upon al-Marwah as he did upon al-Safa, until, when it was the last circuit upon al-Marwah, he said: Had I known beforehand what I know now, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal, and I would have made it Umrah. Whoever of you has no sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram and make it Umrah. Suraqah ibn Ju'shum stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for this year of ours or for ever and ever? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced his fingers one into another and said: Umrah has entered into Hajj - twice - no, rather for ever and ever. Ali came from Yemen with the sacrificial camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found Fatimah among those who had exited ihram; she had worn dyed clothes and applied kohl, so he disapproved of that in her. She said: My father commanded me with this. Ali used to say in Iraq: So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inciting against Fatimah for what she had done, seeking a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning what she mentioned from him. He said: I informed him that I had disapproved of that in her, and he said: She has spoken the truth, she has spoken the truth. He said: What did you say when you assumed Hajj? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger, peace be upon him, enters ihram with. He said: I have the sacrificial animal with me, so do not exit ihram. The total of the sacrificial animals which Ali brought from Yemen and which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought was one hundred. The people all exited ihram and shortened except the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and whoever had a sacrificial animal with him. When it was the day of al-Tarwiyah they headed to Mina and entered ihram for Hajj; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode and prayed there Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr. Then he remained a little until the sun rose, and commanded a tent of hair to be pitched for him at Namirah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out, while Quraysh did not doubt except that he would stand at the Sacred Monument as Quraysh used to do in the pre-Islamic age; but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on until he reached Arafah, found the tent pitched for him at Namirah, and stopped there until, when the sun declined, he commanded al-Qaswa, which was saddled for him. He came to the bottom of the valley and addressed the people, saying: Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you like the sacredness of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Every matter of the pre-Islamic age is placed beneath my feet; the blood of the pre-Islamic age is placed, and the first blood I place of the blood of the children of Adam is the blood of Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith, who was being suckled among Banu Sa'd and Hudhayl killed him; the usury of the pre-Islamic age is placed, and the first usury I place is our usury, the usury of Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, for it is all placed. Fear Allah concerning women, for you have taken them by the trust of Allah and made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah; for you against them is that they do not allow upon your beds anyone you dislike; if they do that, strike them with a striking not severe; for them against you are their provision and clothing in a fitting manner. I have left among you that which you will not go astray after if you hold to it: the Book of Allah. You will be asked about me, so what will you say? They said: We testify that you have conveyed, delivered, and advised. He said with his forefinger, raising it to the sky and pointing it to the people: O Allah, bear witness, three times. Then he called the adhan, then established and prayed Zuhr, then established and prayed Asr, praying nothing between them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode until he reached the standing place; he placed the belly of his camel al-Qaswa toward the rocks, placed the rope of the walkers before him, and faced the qiblah. He remained standing until the sun set and the yellowness departed a little when the disc disappeared; he mounted Usamah behind him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed, having tightened the bridle of al-Qaswa until its head touched the pommel of his saddle, saying with his right hand: O people, calmness, calmness. Whenever he came to a mountain of the mountains he loosened it a little until it ascended. When he reached Muzdalifah he prayed there Maghrib and Isha with one adhan and two iqamahs, glorifying nothing between them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay down until dawn broke; he prayed Fajr when the morning became clear to him, with adhan and iqamah. Then he mounted al-Qaswa until he reached the Sacred Monument; he faced the qiblah, supplicated Him, magnified Him, declared His unity and proclaimed His oneness; he remained standing until it was fully bright. He departed before the sun rose, mounting al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him, who was a man of beautiful hair, fair and handsome. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed, women in litters passed running, and al-Fadl began looking at them; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand upon his face, so al-Fadl turned his face to the other side looking, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved his hand from the other side upon the face of al-Fadl, turning his face from the other side looking, until he reached Muhassir, where he moved a little. Then he took the middle road which leads to the Greater Pillar until he reached the pillar by the tree; he stoned it with seven pebbles, magnifying with each pebble of them like chickpea-sized pebbles, stoning from the bottom of the valley. Then he went to the slaughter place and slaughtered sixty-three camels, then gave to Ali, who slaughtered what remained, associating him in his sacrificial animal. Then he commanded a piece from each camel, so they were placed in a pot, cooked, and they ate of its meat and drank of its broth. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode and hastened to the House, prayed Zuhr at Makkah, and came to Banu Abd al-Muttalib giving water at Zamzam, and said: Draw water, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib; were it not that people would overcome you over your watering, I would have drawn with you. They called a bucket for him, and he drank from it."
"1136","Ibrahim ibn Isa al-Talqani narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Hamzah ibn Hassan, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while upon his pulpit: O people, repent to your Lord before you die, hasten to Him with righteous deeds, join what is between Him and you with frequent remembrance of Him and frequent charity in secret and in public, so that you are rewarded, aided, and provided for. Know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has obligated Friday upon you in this year of mine, in this month of mine, in this hour of mine, as a written obligation; whoever abandons it in my life or after my death until the Day of Resurrection, denying it and belittling its right, while he has a just or an unjust imam, Allah shall not join his affair for him, nor bless him in his matter; indeed he has no prayer, indeed he has no Hajj, indeed he has no charity, indeed he has no zakat, indeed he has no righteousness. Whoever repents, Allah turns to him. Indeed no Bedouin shall lead a migrant in prayer; indeed no woman shall lead a man; indeed no wicked one shall lead a righteous one unless he is a ruler."
"1137","Abu Nu'aym narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How have you risen this morning, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Well, better than a man who has not risen fasting and has not visited a sick person."
"1138","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ka'b ibn Ujrah: May Allah protect you, O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from the rule of the foolish. He said: And what is the rule of the foolish? He said: Rulers after me who lie; they do not guide by my guidance nor follow my practice. Whoever believes them in their lying and aids them in their wrongdoing, those are not of me and I am not of them, nor shall they come to my Pool; and whoever does not believe them in their lying nor aid them in their wrongdoing, those are of me and I am of them, and they shall come to my Pool. O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is a means of nearness - or he said: a proof. O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, no flesh grown of unlawful earnings enters Paradise; the Fire is more entitled to it. O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, people are two travelers: one who buys himself and frees it, and one who sells it and destroys it."
"1139","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Ma'mar informed, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at Tabuk twenty days shortening the prayer."
"1140","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn al-Hakam, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Cover the vessel and tie the waterskin, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has a disease which descends in the year on one night; it does not pass by an uncovered vessel or an untied waterskin except that some of that disease falls into it. [Print apparatus note in source mentions a variant name Ja'far ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam; chain rendered literally as printed.]"
"1141","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he drew a line like this in front of him and said: This is the path of Allah. Then he drew two lines on his right and two lines on his left and said: These are the paths of Satan. Then he placed his hand on the middle line and recited this verse: And that this is My straight path, so follow it, and do not follow the other paths, lest they separate you from His path."
"1142","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Jabir, who said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said to a man on Friday: You have no Friday (reward). The man was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Messenger of Allah, Sa'd said to me: You have no Friday. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why, O Sa'd? He said: He spoke while you were delivering the sermon. He said: Sa'd spoke the truth."
"1143","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of injustice, for it will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you; it drove them to shed their blood and to violate their sacred things."
"1144","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from one of the family of Jabir ibn Abdullah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar and their children and their children's children and their dependents. He said: Whenever fresh dates were in season, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not break his fast except with fresh dates, and when there were no fresh dates, he would not break his fast except with dry dates."
"1145","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Shurahbil, who said: Jabir ibn Abdullah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For one of you to withhold his hand from pebbles is better for him than a hundred black-eyed camels; but if Satan overcomes one of you, let him wipe only once."
"1146","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir al-Ansari, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought two large horned black-and-white castrated rams. He laid one of them down and said: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Most Great; O Allah, on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad. Then he brought the other near, laid it down, and said: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Most Great; on behalf of Muhammad and his ummah, whoever of them bore witness to Your oneness and bore witness to my conveyance of the message."
"1147","Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Shurahbil al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given something and finds means, let him repay it; and whoever does not find means, let him praise him for it, for if he praises him for it he has thanked him, and if he conceals it he has been ungrateful for it. And whoever adorns himself with what he was not given is like one wearing two garments of falsehood."
"1148","Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ya'qub al-Qummi, from Isa, from Jabir, that Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind and I hear the call to prayer. He said: When you hear the call to prayer, then come to it, even if crawling, even if creeping."
"1149","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Ubaydah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: Our dwellings were far, so we wanted to move closer to the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we consulted him. He said: Remain in your dwellings; there is no believer who performs ablution and performs it well, then heads for the mosque, except that Allah records for him a good deed for every step he takes and erases a sin from him."
"1150","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever completes his pilgrimage rites, and the Muslims are safe from his tongue and his hand, will be forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"1151","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Shall I not inform you of something that Nuh enjoined upon his son? Nuh said to his son: O my son, I enjoin upon you two things and forbid you two things. I enjoin you, O my son, to say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, for if the heaven and the earth were placed in one scale they would be outweighed by it, and if they were formed into a ring it would shatter it. And I enjoin you to say: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, for it is the prayer of creation and the glorification of creation, and through it creation is provided for. And I forbid you, O my son, to associate anything with Allah, for whoever associates anything with Allah, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him. And I forbid you, O my son, arrogance, for no one will enter Paradise while there is in his heart even a mustard seed's weight of arrogance. Then Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, is arrogance that one of us has a mount to ride, or sandals to wear, or clothes to wear, or food over which he gathers his companions? He said: No; rather arrogance is to despise the truth and to belittle the believer. And I shall inform you of qualities: whoever has them in him is not arrogant: tying up the sheep, riding the donkey, sitting with the poor among the believers, let one of you eat with his family, and wearing wool."
"1152","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, who said: I came upon Jabir ibn Abdullah in Makkah and found him praying Asr for his companions while sitting. He said: I waited until he gave the salutation, then I said: May Allah forgive you, you are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet you pray with them while sitting? He said: I am ill, so I sat and commanded them to sit and pray with me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man prays Isha in congregation, then prays after it whatever he wishes, then prays witr before he departs, except that that night will be for him as though he met the Night of Decree in answered prayer. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The imam is a shield; if he prays standing, then pray standing, and if he prays sitting, then pray sitting. He said: We used to call out in our homes for the prayer and gather our families."
"1153","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, who said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among his Companions, a funeral passed by him, so we stood to carry it, and behold it was the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it was the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess. He said: Death is a terror, so when you see a funeral, stand."
"1154","Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar narrated to us, Yazid al-Faqir narrated to us, Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given five things that no one before me was given: I have been aided with terror over a month's journey; the earth has been made for me a means of purification and a mosque, so whichever man of my ummah is overtaken by prayer, let him pray; spoils of war have been made lawful for me though they were not lawful for anyone before me; I have been given intercession; and every prophet used to be sent to his people specifically, while I have been sent to mankind generally."
"1155","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Salamah ibn Abi Yazid, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish for death, for the terror of the ascent is severe, and a man's happiness lies in his life being long and Allah granting him repentance."
"1156","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Sabit, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Narrate from the Children of Israel, for there were wonders among them. Then he began to narrate, saying: A group of them went out and came to one of their graveyards and said: If only we prayed two rak'ahs and supplicated Allah Almighty to bring forth for us one of the dead to inform us about death. He said: So they did, and while they were thus, a man raised his head from a grave, between his eyes the mark of prostration, and said: O you people, what did you want from me? By Allah, I died a hundred years ago, and the heat of death has not subsided from me until just now, so supplicate Allah to return me to as I was."
"1157","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you hear the barking of dogs or the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge with Allah, for they see what you do not see. And lessen going out when movement quiets down, for Allah Almighty disperses of His creation what He wills. And close the doors and mention Allah's name over them, for Satan does not open a closed door - and mention Allah's name over it - and cover the large vessels, and overturn the utensils, and tie the mouths of the waterskins."
"1158","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Anas ibn Malik informed me that prayer was enjoined upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night he was taken by night fifty prayers, then it was reduced to five. Then it was called out: O Muhammad, the word is not changed with Me, and indeed for you with the five is fifty."
"1159","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, that Anas ibn Malik informed him, saying: One day we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said: There shall now appear to you from this mountain pass a man of the people of Paradise. Then a man of the Ansar appeared, his beard dripping with water from his ablution, having hung his sandals in his hand by his left. He greeted us. The next day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of that, and that man appeared in the same state as the first time. On the third day, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of his saying, and that man appeared in the same state as the first time. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As followed him and said: I quarreled with my father and swore not to enter upon him for three days, so if you see fit to shelter me with you for three days until the three days pass, do so. He said: Yes. Anas said: Abdullah used to narrate that he stayed with him three nights and did not see him stand in prayer at night at all, except that when he turned restlessly on his bed - or he said: turned over - he remembered Allah Almighty and uttered the takbir until he rose for the dawn prayer. Abdullah ibn Amr said: Except that I heard nothing from him but good. When the three nights had passed, I almost belittled his deeds. I said: O Abdullah, there was no anger nor estrangement between me and my father, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say of you three times: There shall now appear to you a man of the people of Paradise, and you appeared all three times. So I wanted to stay with you to see what your deeds are so that I might follow you, but I did not see you do many deeds. So what is it that raised you to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? He said: It is nothing but what you saw. When I turned away, he called me and said: It is nothing but what you saw, except that I find in myself no deceit toward any Muslim, nor do I envy anyone for any good that Allah Almighty has given him. Abdullah said: I said: It is this that raised you, and it is this that we cannot bear."
"1160","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, saying: There was no one who resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"1161","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from his horse and his right side was grazed. He said: So they came to him and he prayed with them sitting, and he gestured to them to sit. When he gave the salutation, he said: The imam is appointed only to be followed; when he pronounces the takbir, then pronounce the takbir, and when he bows, then bow, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then say: Our Lord, and to You belongs praise, and when he prostrates, then prostrate, and when he prays sitting, then pray sitting all together."
"1162","And with the same chain, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gesture during the prayer."
"1163","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, saying: On Monday, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lifted the curtain of the chamber and saw Abu Bakr praying with the people. He said: I looked at his face as though it were a page of the mushaf, while he was smiling. We almost turned in distraction in our prayer out of joy at seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Abu Bakr wanted to step back, so he gestured to him to remain as you are. Then he let down the curtain, and he passed away that very day. Then Umar stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has not died, but his Lord sent to him as He sent to Musa, who stayed away from his people forty nights. By Allah, I hope the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will live until he cuts off the hands of men among the hypocrites and their tongues who claim - or he said: who say - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died."
"1164","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Hamzah after he had been mutilated and disfigured, and said: Were it not that Safiyyah would feel it in herself, I would have left him until Allah gathers him from the bellies of wild beasts and birds. He was shrouded in a striped garment: when his head was covered his feet showed, and when his feet were covered his head showed, so his head was covered. He did not pray over any of the martyrs, and he said: I am a witness over you today. He would gather two or three in one grave, then ask: Which of them knew most Quran? And he would place him first in the lahd. And he shrouded two or three men in one garment."
"1165","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to me, al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, saying: Uqayl ibn Khalid al-Ayli narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he narrated to him, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out before the sun declined, he would delay Zuhr until the time of Asr, then alight and combine the two; and if the sun declined before he set out, he would pray Zuhr, then mount."
"1166","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I and the Hour have been sent like these two - and he gestured with the middle finger and the index finger."
"1167","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no one who enters Paradise who wishes he returned to the world, even if he had everything upon the back of the earth, except the martyr, for he wishes he returned to the world and was killed ten times, because of the honor he sees."
"1168","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord Almighty says: If My servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; and if he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"1169","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam, if you remember Me within yourself, I remember you within Myself; and if you remember Me in an assembly, I remember you in an assembly of angels - or he said: in an assembly better than them; and if you draw near to Me a handspan, I draw near to you a cubit, and if you draw near to Me a cubit, I draw near to you a fathom, and if you come to Me walking, I come to you hastening. Ma'mar said: Qatadah said: And Allah Almighty is swifter with forgiveness."
"1170","Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the bowing and the prostration, for I see you from behind my back - and perhaps he said: from behind me - when you bow and prostrate."
"1171","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have supplicated Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"1172","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah Almighty says: Bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, with goodness in his heart weighing an atom; bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, with goodness in his heart weighing a grain of barley; bring out of the Fire whoever said: There is no god but Allah, with goodness in his heart weighing a small worm."
"1173","Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to the Byzantines but he was not answered. It was said to him: It is not read unless it is sealed. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver, and he engraved on it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. Anas said: It is as though I am looking at its whiteness on his hand."
"1174","Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother - or for his neighbor - what he loves for himself."
"1175","Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None of you believes until I am dearer to him than his child and his father and all mankind."
"1176","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two straps on his sandals."
"1177","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, who said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Which clothing was most pleasing - or dearest - to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The hibarah (striped Yemeni cloak)."
"1178","Yazid informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not wrong the believer a single good deed he does; he is given for it in this world and rewarded for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is given in this world for the good deeds he did for Allah Almighty, until when he reaches the Hereafter there will be no good deed left with Allah for which he may be given good."
"1179","Rawh ibn Ubadah al-Qaysi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The disbeliever will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: What do you think, if you had the earth filled with gold, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. Then it will be said to him: You have lied; you were asked what was easier than that."
"1180","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: Anas ibn Malik informed us, saying: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him, he hears the striking of their sandals. He said: Two angels come to him and sit him up, and say to him: What did you used to say about this man? He said: As for the believer, he says: I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then it is said to him: Look at your seat in the Fire; Allah has exchanged it for a seat in Paradise for you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And he sees both of them. Qatadah said: And it was mentioned to us that his grave is widened for him seventy cubits, and it is filled with greenery for him until the Day of Resurrection."
"1181","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, how will the disbeliever be gathered upon his face on the Day of Resurrection? The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The One who made him walk on his feet is able to make him walk upon his face in the Fire."
"1182","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hell will continue to say: Is there any more, until the Lord of Might places His foot in it, and it says: Enough, enough, by Your might, and it contracts, part of it to part."
"1183","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"1184","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The people of Makkah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a sign, so the moon split in Makkah twice. Then was revealed: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split, up to His saying: Continuing magic - meaning going away."
"1185","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq on the night he was taken by night, saddled and bridled, but it proved difficult for him. Jibril said to it: Is it with Muhammad that you do this? No one more honored to Allah than him has ridden you. He said: So it broke into sweat."
"1186","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believers will gather on the Day of Resurrection and will be concerned about that Day, and they will say: If only we sought intercession with our Lord until He relieves us from this place of ours. So they will come to Adam and say to him: O Adam, you are the father of mankind; Allah created you with His hand, made His angels prostrate to you, and taught you the names of all things, so intercede for us with our Lord until He relieves us from this place of ours. He will say to them: I am not for that, and he will mention his sin that he committed; but go to Nuh, the first messenger Allah Almighty sent to the people of the earth. So they will come to Nuh, and he will say to them: I am not for that, and he will mention to them his sin that he committed; but go to Ibrahim, the close friend of the Most Merciful. So they will come to Ibrahim, and he will say to them: I am not for that, and he will mention to them his errors that he committed; but go to Musa, a servant to whom Allah gave the Torah and spoke to him directly. So they will come to Musa, and he will say to them: I am not for that, and he will mention to them his sin that he committed; but go to Isa, the Messenger of Allah and His spirit and His word. So they will come to Isa, and he will say: I am not for that, but go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a servant forgiven what preceded of his sin and what followed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and upon all the prophets: So they will come to me, and I shall proceed with them and seek permission from my Lord, and permission will be granted me. When I see my Lord, I shall fall prostrate to Him, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say: O Muhammad, raise your head; ask, you shall be given, and intercede, your intercession shall be accepted. So I shall praise my Lord with praises He has taught me. Then I shall set a limit for them and admit them to Paradise. Then I shall return a second time and seek permission from my Lord, and permission will be granted me. When I see my Lord, I shall fall prostrate to Him, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say: O Muhammad, raise your head; ask, you shall be given, and intercede, your intercession shall be accepted. So I shall praise my Lord with praises He has taught me. Then I shall set a second limit for them and admit them to Paradise. Then I shall return a third time and seek permission from my Lord, and permission will be granted me. When I see my Lord, I shall fall prostrate to Him, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say: O Muhammad, raise your head; ask, you shall be given, and intercede, your intercession shall be accepted. So I shall praise my Lord with praises He has taught me. Then I shall set a third limit for them and admit them to Paradise, until I return and say: O Lord, none remains in the Fire except whom eternity has become due upon or whom the Quran has confined."
"1187","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah and Aban, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: O mankind, fear your Lord; indeed the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on one of his journeys, so he raised his voice with it until his Companions gathered to him. He said: Do you know which day this is? The day Allah Almighty will say to Adam, peace be upon him: O Adam, arise and dispatch the contingent of the Fire: from every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire, and one to Paradise. That weighed heavily upon the Muslims, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aim rightly, draw near, and receive glad tidings; by the One in whose hand is my soul, you among mankind are but like a mole on the side of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast. And with you are two creations: whenever they were with anything, they multiplied it: Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and whoever perished among the disbelievers of men and jinn."
"1188","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that it was revealed to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his return from al-Hudaybiyyah, while his Companions were mingled with grief and gloom, for they had been barred from their rites and had sacrificed the sacrificial animals at al-Hudaybiyyah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There has been revealed to me a verse dearer to me than the whole world. Then he recited it to his Companions, and they said: Congratulations, O Prophet of Allah; Allah has made clear what He will do with you, so what will He do with us? Then Allah Almighty revealed concerning that: That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens, up to: A great triumph."
"1189","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas, concerning His saying: Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a river in Paradise - or the Prophet said: I saw a river in Paradise whose banks were domes of pearl. I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah has granted you."
"1190","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought suhur along with Zayd ibn Thabit. When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his suhur, he rose for the dawn prayer. So we said to Anas: How long was it between his finishing his suhur and his entering his prayer? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"1191","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, and I did not hear any of them recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"1192","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, who said: Anas said to us: I shall narrate to you a hadith that no one will narrate to you after me: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge departs, ignorance appears, wine is drunk, adultery spreads, men decrease, and women increase, until one man will be the caretaker of fifty women."
"1193","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: My Lord has commanded me to recite the Quran to you. Ubayy said: Did He name me to you? He said: And He named you to me. He said: Then Ubayy wept."
"1194","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the funeral of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was carried, the hypocrites said: How light his funeral is - and that was because of his judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The angels were carrying him."
"1195","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that a man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer, and said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Which of you said such and such words? The people fell silent. He said: Which of you said it - three times? The man said: I said it, and I intended by it nothing but good. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twelve angels rushed to take it first, not knowing how to write it, so your Lord Almighty said: Write it as My servant said it."
"1196","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah - meaning from Qatadah - from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky during their prayer? His speech about that grew stern, until he said: They shall desist from that, or their eyesight shall be snatched away."
"1197","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Zayd ibn Hubab al-Ukli narrated to me, from Ali ibn Mas'adah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam errs, and the best of those who err are the repentant."
"1198","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never delivered a sermon except that he said: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness."
"1199","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, Anas narrated to us, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his journeys, with Mu'adh ibn Jabal riding behind him, with nothing between them but the rear of the saddle. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mu'adh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and at your aid. He said: Do you know what Allah Almighty's right over the servants is? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Allah Almighty's right over the servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him. He said: Then do you know what the servants' right upon Allah Almighty is, when they do that? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Their right upon Allah is that He not punish them."
"1200","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to me, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that a fine silk cloak was gifted to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though he used to forbid silk. The people marveled at it, so he said: By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this."
